local E = ns.DB.entries
E["npc:arcanist-doan"] = {t="npc",n="Arcanist Doan",z="scarlet",s="Arcanist Doan is a master human mage residing within the Athenaeum of the Scarlet Monastery's Library wing. Formerly an associate of the Silver Hand who assisted in forging the legendary Ashbringer, he now serves the Scarlet Crusade as one of its most lethal arcane specialists and guardian of key crusade archives.",h="Arcanist Doan is a master human mage residing within the Athenaeum of the Scarlet Monastery's Library wing.",sec={{t="A Mage Among Paladins",b="Before the Scarlet Crusade turned inward and zealous, Arcanist Doan walked among the Knights of the Silver Hand. During the Third War, he met with Highlord Alexandros Mograine and other founders at Southshore. When Mograine revealed a shadowy crystal taken from an orc warlock during the Second War, Doan observed its unnatural ability to absorb holy energy. Joining his arcane insight with the holy magic of his peers, Doan helped cleanse the void crystal into radiant light, forming the heart of the weapon known as the Ashbringer.",sp=0},{t="Defense of Hearthglen",b="As the Scourge swept across Lordaeron, Doan advocated for total plague containment. When the undead battered Hearthglen's fortifications, he held the ramparts alongside High Inquisitor Isillien. While others urged him to unleash magic immediately, Doan methodically gathered his strength, unleashing a devastating blizzard at the precise moment necessary to shatter the advancing undead ranks. His clinical patience proved his lethal mastery of battlefield evocation.",sp=0},{t="Keeper of the Athenaeum",b="While the fanatical ranks of the Scarlet Crusade lean heavily on martial fury and holy fervor, Doan remained convinced that raw arcane power was essential to purging the Scourge from Lordaeron. Stationed deep inside the Athenaeum of the Monastery's library, he was entrusted as both a lorekeeper and an operational gatekeeper, safeguarding the Scarlet Key that secures crusade sanctuaries across the northern kingdoms.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is a mage in the Scarlet Crusade?",a="Although the Crusade is dominated by zealot paladins and priests, Doan has been allied with its founders since the Silver Hand days. He firmly believes that masterwork arcane magic is an indispensable weapon needed to cleanse the Scourge from Lordaeron.",al={"why is doan a mage","crusade mage","doan magic"},it="side"},{q="What is Arcanist Doan's connection to the Ashbringer?",a="At a council in Southshore during the Third War, Alexandros Mograine presented an orb of darkness taken from an orc warlock. Doan helped direct the magical experiment where the Silver Hand poured their magic into the relic, successfully purifying it into the radiant core that forged the Ashbringer.",al={"doan ashbringer","did doan make ashbringer","ashbringer crystal"},it="ties"},{q="What does Doan guard in the Library?",a="Doan keeps watch over the Monastery's repository of books and historical records in the Athenaeum. Behind him sits a lockbox containing the Scarlet Key, an essential key that opens the locked gates to the Monastery's Armory and Cathedral wings.",al={"what does doan drop","scarlet key","why kill doan"},it="why_here"},{q="What magic does Doan use in combat?",a="Doan blends abjuration and evocation magic. He is famous for casting an Arcane Bubble that renders him invulnerable while he channels a massive, room-engulfing Detonation spell. He also disrupts spellcasters with area silences and polymorphs threats into sheep.",al={"doan spells","doan abilities","arcanist doan bubble"},it="power"},{q="Where did Doan fight during the Third War?",a="Beyond attending the pivotal war councils in Southshore, Doan fought on the front lines at Hearthglen, using catastrophic blizzard spells from the ramparts to break massive undead assault waves.",al={"doan war history","doan hearthglen","where was doan"},it="history"},{q="Does Doan harbor any personal secrets?",a="Doan is said to have held an unrequited affection for Brigitte Abbendis, daughter of General Abbendis, while running with the early crusade leaders.",al={"doan dalaran fountain","doan abbendis","doan lore"}},{q="Who is Arcanist Doan?",a="Arcanist Doan is a human mage and one of the most powerful arcane practitioners serving the Scarlet Crusade. Formerly aligned with the Knights of the Silver Hand during the Third War, he stood alongside heroes like Alexandros Mograine and helped purify the dark crystal that forged the Ashbringer. Today, he resides deep within the Athenaeum of the Scarlet Monastery's Library, wielding devastating arcane magic in defense of the order's holy sanctuary.",al={"who is doan","arcanist doan lore","doan scarlet monastery"},it="identity",add=true},{q="What does Arcanist Doan want?",a="Doan is driven by the conviction that arcane magic is the only true way to completely cleanse Lordaeron of the Scourge. While his Scarlet Crusade brethren rely almost entirely upon the zealotry of the Holy Light, Doan believes raw arcane power and study are necessary to contain and eradicate the undead plague once and for all.",al={"doan goals","what does doan want","arcanist doan motive"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Arcanist Doan feared?",a="Doan is feared as one of the most formidable mages in Lordaeron, renowned for masterfully blending Evocation and Abjuration magic. He perfected a technique that encases himself in a nearly impenetrable Arcane Bubble to channel cataclysmic Detonation spells, capable of incinerating entire groups of intruders in an instant.",al={"why is doan feared","how strong is doan","doan reputation"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Scholars of the arcane recognize Doan from 'The Schools of Arcane Magic: Abjuration,' where his ability to combine shielding with evocation to cast an impenetrable bubble is cited as an exceptionally rare feat.",["class:Paladin"]="Doan fought beside the founding members of the Silver Hand and was directly involved in purifying the crystal that created the Ashbringer before joining the crusade's descent into zealotry.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance forces, Doan represents what remains of Lordaeron's proud Kirin Tor and Silver Hand defenders who abandoned reason in favor of the Crusade's violent paranoia.",["faction:Horde"]="The Forsaken and their Horde allies see Doan as a dangerous Scarlet commander whose library shelters vital intelligence and keys needed to breach the Crusade's inner sanctums."},kw={"arcanist","ashbringer","athenaeum","detonation","doan","hearthglen","library","scarlet key","scarlet monastery"},rel={"subzone:scarlet-monastery-library","zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","subzone:hearthglen","subzone:southshore","topic:scourge"},src={"Arcanist Doan"}}
E["npc:bloodmage-thalnos"] = {t="npc",n="Bloodmage Thalnos",z="scarlet",s="Bloodmage Thalnos is a skeletal spellcaster who haunts the Graveyard wing of the Scarlet Monastery. Once a sadistic interrogator within the Scarlet Crusade, he succumbed to the plague of undeath he fanatically fought against, yet he remains entrenched deep within their holy grounds.",h="Bloodmage Thalnos is a skeletal spellcaster who haunts the Graveyard wing of the Scarlet Monastery.",sec={{t="The Inquisitor's Fall",b="Within the zealous ranks of the Scarlet Crusade, Thalnos earned dark notoriety for his brutal methods of torture, used under the guise of purifying prospective recruits of taint. Yet despite his fanatical devotion to rooting out corruption, the sadistic mage ultimately succumbed to the plague of undeath. Rather than being cleansed or permanently destroyed, he rose as a withered skeleton, still clinging to his fiery magic and arcane mastery.",sp=0},{t="Master of the Graveyard",b="Confined to the deepest corner of the monastery's courtyard tombs, Thalnos commands apparitions and shambling undead minions against anyone who disturbs his domain. His continued presence poses a bitter contradiction for the Crusade: an undead monstrosity lingering right beneath their sacred halls, embodying the very horror they swore an eternity to eradicate.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bloodmage Thalnos?",a="Thalnos was once a cruel inquisitor and mage of the Scarlet Crusade who used horrific torture to test recruits for corruption. Ironically, he contracted the plague of undeath himself and transformed into a skeletal spellcaster haunting the Monastery's graveyard.",al={"who is thalnos","thalnos lore","bloodmage thalnos info"},it="identity"},{q="Why is an undead skeleton allowed in the Scarlet Monastery?",a="The Crusade fanatically executes all undead on sight, making Thalnos's survival anomalous. Stowed away at the far end of the Graveyard amidst risen crypts and spirits, he prowls his own blighted domain rather than walking freely among the living crusaders.",al={"why is thalnos in monastery","why does scarlet crusade keep thalnos","scarlet crusade undead mage"},it="why_here"},{q="What powers does Thalnos wield?",a="Despite retaining the title of Bloodmage and rising as a skeleton, Thalnos commands fiery spells, shadow magic, and summons vengeful spirits and walking dead to overwhelm trespassers in the graveyard.",al={"thalnos spells","bloodmage thalnos magic","what does thalnos do"},it="power"},{q="Was Thalnos a blood elf?",a="His title suggests arcane blood magic traditions often tied to high elves or blood elves, and the Crusade has occasionally included elven members. However, as an animated skeleton stripped of flesh and features, his original mortal lineage remains uncertain.",al={"is thalnos high elf","thalnos race","what race was thalnos"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants Thalnos dead?",a="Both Forsaken agents and dissident voices seek his destruction. Those dispatching adventurers to end him are often shocked and baffled to learn that a high-ranking Scarlet inquisitor has become an undead skeleton.",al={"thalnos quest","who wants thalnos killed","the dark side of the light thalnos"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Whose side is Bloodmage Thalnos on?",a="Thalnos was once a torturer for the Scarlet Crusade, but after succumbing to the plague of undeath, he became a creature entirely driven by vengeance and unholy power. Now an undead skeleton, he fiercely guards his own domain within the monastery's graveyard, commanding apparitions and zombified creatures to slaughter any living trespassers who cross his path.",al={"thalnos faction","who does thalnos serve","is thalnos scarlet crusade"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Bloodmage Thalnos want?",a="Driven mad by cruelty and the trauma of contracting undeath, Thalnos desires little more than unholy vengeance. Bound to the monastery's graveyard, the vengeful skeletal mage commands restless apparitions and reanimated corpses to eradicate anyone who dares enter his cursed territory.",al={"what does thalnos want","thalnos goal","thalnos motives"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Bloodmage Thalnos feared?",a="Thalnos gained widespread notoriety within the Scarlet Crusade for his sheer sadism. Long before he fell to undeath, he used excruciating torture methods to violently \"purify\" incoming recruits. That terrifying reputation only grew darker when he succumbed to the plague and rose again as a ruthless skeletal bloodmage.",al={"why is thalnos feared","what made thalnos famous","bloodmage thalnos reputation"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Thalnos represents the catastrophic corruption of arcane ambition when entwined with fanatical madness and the plague.",["faction:Horde"]="The Forsaken view Thalnos as living proof of the Scarlet Crusade's hypocritical madness—a monster who tortured others for taint only to succumb to the very undeath he reviled.",["class:Priest"]="Standing amidst the tombs, Thalnos is an unsettling testament to how easily zealotry and torture invite darkness instead of divine grace."},kw={"bloodmage","graveyard","inquisitor","scarlet monastery","skeleton","thalnos"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:light"},src={"Bloodmage Thalnos"}}
E["npc:herod"] = {t="npc",n="Herod",z="scarlet",s="Herod is a renowned champion and berserker of the Scarlet Crusade, commanding the Armory within the Scarlet Monastery. Known for his ferocious martial prowess and unyielding zeal, he trains recruits in the brutal melee combat needed to wage holy war. His death is sought by both Alliance dissidents and the Horde's rulers in Undercity to weaken the Crusade's military core.",h="Herod is a renowned champion and berserker of the Scarlet Crusade, commanding the Armory within the Scarlet...",sec={{t="The Champion of the Armory",b="Within the fortified halls of the Scarlet Monastery's Armory, Herod stands as the embodiment of the Crusade's martial aggression. Unlike the spellcasters and paladins who channel holy magic in the Cathedral, Herod relies on raw, bloodthirsty physical power. Clad in mail and wielding a massive two-handed axe, he personally trains cohorts of Scarlet Trainees, instilling a furious devotion to exterminating anyone not allied with their fanatical cause.",sp=0},{t="A High-Priority Target",b="Because Herod oversees the armaments and martial training of the Crusade's front-line warriors, taking him down is essential for anyone seeking to dismantle the order. Raleigh the Devout, an ex-Crusader disillusioned with the order's madness residing in Southshore, calls for Herod's demise to shatter their military leadership. Across Lordaeron, the dreadlord Varimathras in the Undercity similarly seeks his execution to clear out a dangerous human bastion bordering Forsaken territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Herod?",a="Herod is an elite human warrior and commander of the Armory in the Scarlet Monastery. He serves as one of the four principal leaders of the Monastery, responsible for outfitting and drilling the Crusade's zealous melee fighters.",al={"herod lore","who is herod","herod scarlet monastery"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Herod located?",a="Herod can be found at the heart of the Armory wing in the Scarlet Monastery, situated in northeastern Tirisfal Glades. He awaits challengers in a central training ring surrounded by viewing galleries.",al={"where is herod","herod location","find herod"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the Horde want Herod dead?",a="The dreadlord Varimathras, acting on behalf of the Forsaken in the Undercity, seeks the elimination of the Monastery's key commanders—including Herod—to eradicate the Crusade's lingering threat right on the Forsaken capital's doorstep.",al={"varimathras herod quest","why horde kill herod","into the scarlet monastery"},it="motive"},{q="Why does the Alliance want Herod dead?",a="Raleigh the Devout, a former member of the Scarlet Crusade stationed in Hillsbrad Foothills, recognizes that the order has descended into fanatical zealotry. He asks Alliance champions to purge Herod to strip the Crusade of its brutal warrior leadership.",al={"in the name of the light","raleigh the devout herod","why alliance kill herod"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when Herod is defeated?",a="Upon Herod's defeat, a mob of young Scarlet Trainees surges out from the surrounding barracks into the ring to avenge their master, illustrating the sheer depth of devotion he fostered in his students.",al={"scarlet trainees","herod trainee rush","herod death event"},sp=1,gp=true},{q="What kind of fighter is Herod?",a="Herod is a berserker and warrior rather than a traditional holy paladin. He uses vicious charges and sweeping whirlwind strikes to pulverize foes, relying on sheer physical frenzy over spells of the Holy Light.",al={"herod fighting style","is herod a paladin"},it="power"},{q="Whose side is Herod on?",a="Herod is a high-ranking commander of the Scarlet Crusade, serving as one of the four key leaders stationed within the Scarlet Monastery. Fanatically loyal to the Crusade's zealous mission, he directs their military training and armory against any and all whom the Crusade deems impure or hostile.",al={"herod faction","who does herod serve","what side is herod on"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Herod want?",a="Herod is dedicated to preparing the Scarlet Crusade's next generation of warriors to eradicate their enemies. Overseeing the Armory, he drills trainees to match his own relentless martial fervor, seeking to crush anyone foolish enough to trespass upon the Monastery's sacred grounds.",al={"herod goal","herod purpose","what is herod trying to do"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Herod here?",a="Herod commands the Armory wing of the Scarlet Monastery. As the champion and trainer of the Scarlet trainees, he oversees the Crusade's arsenal and personally tests anyone who dares challenge the Crusade's heartland.",al={"why is herod in the armory","why is herod at scarlet monastery","herod armory role"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Herod tied to?",a="Herod stands alongside the inner leadership of the Scarlet Monastery, which includes High Inquisitor Whitemane, Scarlet Commander Mograine, and Houndmaster Loksey. Together, they govern the Crusade's bastion in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"who leads herod","herod allies","who does herod work with"},it="ties",add=true},{q="Why is Herod famous or feared?",a="Known as the Scarlet Champion, Herod is renowned for his ferocious, berserker fighting style. Wielding a massive battleaxe, he is infamous for spinning into a devastating, unstoppable whirlwind of steel that rends all nearby foes to pieces.",al={"why is herod feared","herod reputation","what makes herod dangerous"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="Herod is a prime example of an enraged warrior whose furious whirlwind strikes and reckless aggression make him a feared martial paragon among the Scarlet Crusade's recruits.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde and the Forsaken in particular, eliminating Herod directly fulfills Varimathras's orders to break the leadership threatening the borders of Tirisfal Glades.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance heroes who answer Raleigh the Devout's plea can witness firsthand how the once-noble defenders of Lordaeron have fallen into deranged, fanatical bloodlust under leaders like Herod."},kw={"armory","berserker","herod","raleigh the devout","ravager","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","varimathras"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","npc:varimathras","zone:hillsbrad","zone:undercity","topic:light"},src={"Herod"}}
E["npc:high-inquisitor-fairbanks"] = {t="npc",n="High Inquisitor Fairbanks",z="scarlet",s="High Inquisitor Fairbanks was once a revered priest of the Knights of the Silver Hand and a trusted advisor to Highlord Alexandros Mograine. Once a prominent spiritual leader among Lordaeron's surviving defenders, his fate became tied to the dark descent of the Scarlet Crusade.",h="High Inquisitor Fairbanks was once a revered priest of the Knights of the Silver Hand and a trusted advisor...",sec={{t="Advisor to the Ashbringer",b="Before the fall of Lordaeron, Fairbanks was a respected holy man among the Knights of the Silver Hand. When Highlord Alexandros Mograine convened a fateful gathering at the Southshore inn, Fairbanks stood beside him, helping channel holy power into the enigmatic crystal that would eventually become the heart of the legendary Ashbringer. When Prince Arthas dissolved the paladin order, Fairbanks accompanied Mograine to Ironforge, standing witness as King Magni Bronzebeard forged the great blade to combat the Scourge.",sp=0},{t="Betrayal at Stratholme",b="Fairbanks accompanied Alexandros Mograine when the Highlord's eldest son, Renault, led them into a terrible Scourge ambush outside Stratholme. Fairbanks fell early under the press of undead claws, buried beneath piles of rotting corpses. From this horrific vantage, he silently witnessed Renault seize the fallen Ashbringer and plunge it into his own father's heart, corrupting the holy blade with patricide. Surviving the slaughter, Fairbanks clawed his way out from under the dead and fled back to Hearthglen to expose Renault's treachery.",sp=1},{t="Execution and Exile",b="Fairbanks's desperate warnings shattered the remaining defenders of Lordaeron. Those who believed his horrific account abandoned the fanatical order to form the Argent Dawn. Those who remained loyal to Renault and Saidan Dathrohan branded Fairbanks a blasphemer and a lunatic. Infected by the plague during his time buried under Scourge corpses, Fairbanks was quietly executed by the Scarlet Crusade. Rather than granting him a holy burial, the crusaders discarded his body in a hidden chamber behind the Cathedral's altar, where he eventually rose as the very monstrosity they swore to cleanse.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Where can I find High Inquisitor Fairbanks?",a="Fairbanks is hidden inside the Cathedral wing of the Scarlet Monastery. To reach him, enter the side chapel to the right of the main altar and pull a concealed wall torch, which swings open a secret stone doorway leading into a secluded crypt.",al={"where is fairbanks","how to find fairbanks","fairbanks secret room","monastery secret door"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Fairbanks an undead creature?",a="During the ambush at Stratholme, Fairbanks was buried alive beneath piles of Scourge corpses, which infected him with the plague of undeath. After the Scarlet Crusade executed him for his accusations against its leaders, his cast-aside body eventually succumbed to the infection and reanimated in secret.",al={"why is fairbanks a zombie","is fairbanks scourge","why is fairbanks undead"},sp=2,it="origin"},{q="Who was Fairbanks before he was executed?",a="Fairbanks was a devout priest of the Knights of the Silver Hand and the chief counselor to Highlord Alexandros Mograine. He helped purify the crystal that formed the Ashbringer and stood as one of the original spiritual leaders of Lordaeron's surviving defenders.",al={"fairbanks backstory","who is high inquisitor fairbanks","fairbanks lore"},it="identity"},{q="What caused the split between the Scarlet Crusade and the Argent Dawn?",a="When Fairbanks returned from Stratholme and reported what he had witnessed there, the order fractured. Those who believed Fairbanks and rejected Renault's fanaticism walked away to establish the Argent Dawn, while Renault's zealots stayed with the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"argent dawn origin","why did argent dawn split","fairbanks argent dawn"},sp=2,it="conflict"},{q="Why did the Scarlet Crusade kill Fairbanks?",a="The leadership of the Scarlet Crusade branded his testimony of what happened at Stratholme as malicious blasphemy. Furthermore, seeing him exhibit early symptoms of the plague from his wounds at Stratholme, the crusaders murdered him to silence the truth.",al={"why did scarlet kill fairbanks","who killed fairbanks","fairbanks execution"},sp=2,it="history"},{q="Who replaced Fairbanks as High Inquisitor?",a="Following Fairbanks's execution and secret imprisonment, Sally Whitemane ascended to the role of High Inquisitor, presiding over the Scarlet Monastery's inquisitorial interrogations alongside Commander Renault Mograine.",al={"who is high inquisitor now","fairbanks replacement","who succeeded fairbanks"},it="leader"},{q="Whose side is High Inquisitor Fairbanks on now?",a="Fairbanks belongs to no faction anymore. While he was once a revered priest of the Silver Hand and Highlord Alexandros Mograine's closest confidant, his murder and subsequent rise into undeath stripped him of his mind and former allegiances. Consumed by the plague of undeath and locked away by the very zealots he once guided, he is utterly hostile to any living being that enters his hidden tomb, lashing out in mindless agony and madness.",al={"fairbanks faction","is fairbanks hostile","fairbanks side"},sp=1,it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Fairbanks hidden in the Scarlet Monastery?",a="After surviving Renault Mograine's betrayal at Stratholme, Fairbanks returned to expose Renault's patricide to the zealots at Hearthglen. Branded a heretic and liar by Renault and Saidan Dathrohan, Fairbanks was executed to bury the truth. Because he had already begun showing symptoms of the undead plague from being buried under corpses in Stratholme, the Crusaders discarded his body in a hidden chamber behind the Cathedral altar, leaving his reanimated corpse sealed away in secret.",al={"why is fairbanks in the monastery","fairbanks hidden room why","fairbanks secret chamber"},sp=2,it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who was High Inquisitor Fairbanks tied to?",a="Fairbanks was the closest advisor and companion to Highlord Alexandros Mograine, the legendary Ashbringer. Alongside Mograine, Abbendis, and Isillien, he helped cleanse the dark crystal that forged the Ashbringer blade. He accompanied Alexandros to Stratholme, where he witnessed Mograine's own son, Renault, murder his father. His desperate efforts to warn the other knights of Renault's treachery directly inspired the righteous schism that broke away to found the Argent Dawn.",al={"fairbanks connections","fairbanks mograine","who did fairbanks serve"},sp=1,it="ties",add=true}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Fairbanks witnessed the darkest hour of the Silver Hand: the day an honored paladin turned a legendary holy blade against his own father.",["class:Priest"]="Before his fall, Fairbanks channeled the Holy Light alongside Mograine to cleanse the dark orb that became the Ashbringer.",["race:Undead"]="Fairbanks proves the ultimate hypocrisy of the Scarlet Crusade: hiding one of their own plague-ridden dead behind an altar while burning innocent Forsaken.",["faction:Alliance"]="Fairbanks's tragedy traces back to the fallen kingdom of Lordaeron, where the remnants of the Grand Alliance split into zealots and outcasts."},kw={"ashbringer","cathedral","fairbanks","hearthglen","inquisitor","mograine","renault","scarlet monastery","silver hand","stratholme"},rel={"subzone:scarlet-monastery-cathedral","zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","topic:argent-dawn","subzone:stratholme","npc:magni-bronzebeard","npc:tirion-fordring"},src={"High Inquisitor Fairbanks"}}
E["npc:houndmaster-loksey"] = {t="npc",n="Houndmaster Loksey",z="scarlet",s="Houndmaster Loksey is the officer charged with breeding and training the fearsome war dogs of the Scarlet Crusade. Stationed in the kennels within the Scarlet Monastery's Armory, he directs packs of hounds to hunt down undead, intruders, and perceived heretics. His merciless discipline has made the Monastery's beasts infamous throughout Tirisfal Glades.",h="Houndmaster Loksey is the officer charged with breeding and training the fearsome war dogs of the Scarlet...",sec={{t="Master of the Kennels",b="Within the heavily fortified walls of the Scarlet Monastery, Houndmaster Loksey commands the training of vicious tracking and attack dogs. The Scarlet Crusade relies on these trained hounds to sniff out plague-tainted corpses, uncover hidden infiltrators, and run down any survivors fleeing the zealots' wrath. Loksey holds absolute authority over the Armory's kennel wing, ensuring his charges are primed to tear intruders apart limb by limb.",sp=0},{t="Family Rivalry",b="Loksey is not the only beast handler in his family serving the cause. His brother, Huntsman Leopold, serves as the Scarlet Crusade's envoy to the Argent Dawn at Light's Hope Chapel. Leopold holds a low opinion of his brother, privately asserting that Loksey can barely manage his own hounds, let alone represent the order in high-stakes diplomacy. Despite Leopold's scorn, Loksey remains a key officer within the Monastery's inner hierarchy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Houndmaster Loksey be found?",a="Houndmaster Loksey is located inside the Armory wing of the Scarlet Monastery in northeastern Tirisfal Glades, surrounded by his attack dogs within the kennels.",al={"loksey location","where is loksey","houndmaster loksey location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Loksey serve in the Scarlet Crusade?",a="He is the chief animal handler and houndmaster for the Scarlet Crusade at the Monastery, responsible for breeding, conditioning, and directing the war dogs used to sniff out undead and hunt down intruders.",al={"what does loksey do","loksey job","houndmaster duty"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Huntsman Leopold to Loksey?",a="Huntsman Leopold is Loksey's brother. Leopold represents the Scarlet Crusade at Light's Hope Chapel and looks down on Loksey, claiming Loksey cannot properly manage his hounds or handle diplomatic responsibilities.",al={"leopold loksey brother","who is leopold","loksey brother"},it="ties"},{q="Why does the Scarlet Crusade use hounds?",a="The Crusade trains vicious hounds to track down the Scourge and Forsaken through scent, as well as to guard the Monastery's grounds and tear fleeing enemies to pieces.",al={"why dogs","scarlet hounds purpose","crusade dogs"}},{q="Is Loksey considered a leader of the Scarlet Monastery?",a="Yes, Loksey is recognized as one of the key commanding figures in the Scarlet Monastery's military structure, overseeing the critical kennel operations within the Armory.",al={"is loksey a boss","loksey rank","how important is loksey"},it="leader"},{q="Are the hounds dangerous on their own?",a="Yes. Bred for aggression and conditioned by Loksey, the Monastery's war hounds are fierce predators capable of ripping an armored intruder limb from limb in moments.",al={"are dogs strong","scarlet hounds danger","loksey pets"},it="danger"},{q="Who is Houndmaster Loksey?",a="Houndmaster Loksey is a human captain and one of the four commanders residing within the Scarlet Monastery. Renowned for his brutal discipline, he serves as the kennel master responsible for breeding, conditioning, and unleashing the Crusade's vicious hounds upon intruders and suspected carriers of the undead taint.",al={"who is loksey","houndmaster loksey identity","who is houndmaster loksey"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Houndmaster Loksey on?",a="Loksey is staunchly devoted to the Scarlet Crusade, serving as a frontline commander within their monastery stronghold. He shares the Crusade's fanatical hatred for the undead and anyone outside their zealot order, viewing any who encroach upon their halls as interlopers fit only to feed his kennel.",al={"loksey faction","houndmaster loksey alliance","who does loksey serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Houndmaster Loksey want?",a="Loksey aims to defend the Scarlet Monastery by training ruthless hunting packs capable of tearing any enemy apart limb by limb. He wants to scour every trace of the undead and protect Crusade territory from outsiders, using his beasts to hunt down intruders without hesitation or mercy.",al={"loksey goal","what is loksey trying to do","houndmaster loksey motive"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Houndmaster Loksey here?",a="Loksey is stationed in the Monastery's library wing to oversee the Crusader kennels. As houndmaster, he must ensure the hounds remain sharp, aggressively conditioned, and ready to be loosed at a moment's notice to patrol the grounds and slaughter intruders.",al={"why is loksey at the monastery","why is houndmaster loksey here","loksey purpose"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Why is Houndmaster Loksey famous or feared?",a="Loksey is feared for his pack of trained hounds, beasts known to overpower and tear victims to shreds within minutes. Anyone venturing into the monastery dreads encountering his kennel, knowing Loksey's vicious command turns his animals into unrelenting engines of carnage.",al={"why is loksey feared","loksey reputation","why is houndmaster loksey dangerous"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Loksey exemplifies a brutal, aggressive approach to beast training, bending fierce hounds to obey zealotry rather than forging a bond of mutual respect.",["race:Undead"]="Forsaken intruders must beware Loksey's hounds, which are trained specifically to catch the scent of dead flesh and alert the Crusade's garrisons."},kw={"armory","houndmaster loksey","hounds","huntsman leopold","kennels","loksey","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","topic:argent-dawn","topic:alliance"},src={"Houndmaster Loksey"}}
E["npc:interrogator-vishas"] = {t="npc",n="Interrogator Vishas",z="scarlet",s="Interrogator James Vishas is the Scarlet Crusade's master of torment, stationed deep within the Scarlet Monastery's Graveyard wing. Infamous for his shrill voice and sheer cruelty, he takes twisted pleasure in breaking captives and testing the limits of mortal flesh. Few who enter his torture chambers ever leave with their minds or bodies intact.",h="Interrogator James Vishas is the Scarlet Crusade's master of torment, stationed deep within the Scarlet...",sec={{t="The Grand Inquisitor's Scalpel",b="Within the dark crypts and burial grounds of the Scarlet Monastery, Interrogator Vishas tends to the Crusade's captive enemies. While the zealots outside march in gleaming armor under banners of purity, Vishas represents the grim reality behind their crusade: unbridled sadism cloaked in religious righteous fury. He approaches interrogation not merely as an intelligence duty, but as a prized craft, reveling in the agony of Forsaken captives, captured Scourge, and any living travelers unlucky enough to be branded heretics.",sp=0},{t="A Life of Quiet Domesticity",b="Behind the bloody aprons and screams of the torture chamber, Vishas leads a bizarrely domestic double life. Outside the monastery walls, his family—including his wife, Nancy Vishas, and his elder relative Grandpa Vishas—resides peacefully in an isolated cottage on the eastern shores of Lordamere Lake in the Alterac Mountains. Vishas even carries gruesome tokens from his victims back into his personal life, having stripped a captive human named Vorrel Sengutz of his cherished wedding ring to present it as a gift to Nancy.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can Interrogator Vishas be found?",a="Interrogator Vishas is located deep inside the Graveyard wing of the Scarlet Monastery, in Tirisfal Glades. He oversees a grim torture chamber lined with iron cages and bloodied racks.",al={"vishas location","where is interrogator vishas","vishas room"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Vishas torture his prisoners?",a="While the Scarlet Crusade justifies tormenting captives to root out Scourge corruption and extract information, Vishas personally delights in the pain he causes. He takes enormous personal pride in his cruelty, viewing torture as his artistic craft.",al={"why is vishas torturing people","vishas motivation"},it="wants"},{q="Who is Vorrel Sengutz?",a="Vorrel Sengutz is a captive imprisoned and brutally tortured by Vishas inside the Monastery's Graveyard. Vishas subjected Vorrel to weeks of pain and stole his wedding band, intending it as a gift for his wife.",al={"vorrel sengutz prisoner","who is the prisoner in the cage"},it="target"},{q="Where does Vishas' family live?",a="His family lives far from the Monastery, at an unassuming cottage situated along the eastern bank of Lordamere Lake in the Alterac Mountains. His wife Nancy and Grandpa Vishas dwell there quietly, seemingly detached from his atrocities.",al={"nancy vishas location","grandpa vishas","vishas family house"},it="ties"},{q="Does Vishas only torture the undead?",a="No. Although he particularly enjoys tormenting captured undead, the Scarlet Crusade views nearly all outsiders as infected or traitorous. Living humans and Alliance sympathizers like Vorrel Sengutz suffer the exact same agonizing fate under his knives.",al={"who does vishas torture","does vishas attack humans"}},{q="What is Vishas' voice and demeanor like?",a="Vishas is infamous among those who face him for his grating, high-pitched voice, cackling laughter, and disturbing excitement whenever an opportunity presents itself to rip secrets from an unwilling victim.",al={"vishas voice","vishas personality"},it="fame"},{q="Who is Interrogator Vishas?",a="James Vishas is the chief interrogator of the Scarlet Crusade, stationed within the depths of the Scarlet Monastery's Graveyard. Fanatical and notoriously cruel, he takes immense pride in breaking prisoners brought before him. Armed with torture implements and an unhinged zeal, he extracts confessions and torment in equal measure from anyone unfortunate enough to fall into his hands.",al={"who is vishas","interrogator vishas lore","who is james vishas"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Interrogator Vishas on?",a="Vishas is entirely devoted to the Scarlet Crusade. He serves their zealous crusade by torturing suspected Scourge agents, Forsaken prisoners, and anyone else deemed tainted or hostile to the order's fanatical purity.",al={"vishas faction","who does vishas work for","vishas scarlet crusade"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Interrogator Vishas here?",a="Vishas is stationed in the torture chambers of the Scarlet Monastery Graveyard to handle prisoners captured across Tirisfal Glades. He spends his days and nights extracting information, venting sadistic urges, and breaking the spirits of captives like Vorrel Sengutz on behalf of the Crusade.",al={"why is vishas in the graveyard","vishas monastery role","what is vishas doing here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Vishas embodies the hypocritical malice of the living zealots, torturing captured undead out of pure spite while claiming to serve the Holy Light.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance heroes who discover Vishas' work quickly realize that the Scarlet Crusade no longer distinguishes between Scourge monsters and innocent living travelers.",["class:Priest"]="Seeing Vishas invoke zealotry to sanctify horrific mutilation offers a chilling demonstration of how holy purpose can curdle into twisted madness."},kw={"graveyard","interrogator vishas","james vishas","lordamere lake","nancy vishas","scarlet monastery","torture","vorrel sengutz"},rel={"subzone:scarlet-monastery-graveyard","zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:lordamere-lake","zone:alterac","topic:light"},src={"Interrogator Vishas"}}
E["npc:sally-whitemane"] = {t="npc",n="Sally Whitemane",z="scarlet",s="Sally Whitemane is the High Inquisitor of the Scarlet Crusade, presiding over the Cathedral of the Scarlet Monastery. A powerful priestess of the Holy Light, her consuming hatred for the undead drives the Crusade's uncompromising zealotry. Together with Scarlet Commander Renault Mograine, she directs the order's military and ideological campaigns across Lordaeron.",h="Sally Whitemane is the High Inquisitor of the Scarlet Crusade, presiding over the Cathedral of the Scarlet...",sec={{t="Tragedy in Lordaeron",b="Sally Whitemane spent her youth in Southshore alongside childhood companions Renault Mograine and James Vishas. That innocence vanished during the Third War when her family traveled north through Lordaeron and succumbed to the plague of undeath. Forced to personally put down her own parents and siblings after they rose as mindless Scourge minions, Whitemane was left consumed by guilt, grief, and unyielding rage. From that day onward, she dedicated her life solely to eradicating undeath in all its forms.",sp=0},{t="High Inquisitor of the Crusade",b="Rising rapidly through the Scarlet Crusade's hierarchy, Whitemane became its High Inquisitor and took command of the Scarlet Monastery's grand Cathedral. Renowned for her fearsome mastery of Holy magic, she led relief forces to rescue Hearthglen from the Scourge and stood as a guiding hand during the induction of high-ranking Crusaders like Taelan Fordring. Her absolute conviction has made her one of the Crusade's foremost symbols, wielding the Light as an unrelenting weapon against any deemed unclean.",sp=0},{t="Targets in the Cathedral",b="By 25 ADP, Whitemane's fanaticism has drawn enemies from both factions. In Southshore, Raleigh the Devout believes the Crusade has strayed irreparably into corruption and madness, calling for the elimination of Whitemane and Mograine to restore the order's founding virtues. Meanwhile, within the Undercity, the dreadlord Varimathras orchestrates strikes against the Monastery to crush the zealots operating directly on the Forsaken's doorstep.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Sally Whitemane?",a="Sally Whitemane is the High Inquisitor of the Scarlet Crusade. She commands the order's spiritual and inquisitorial efforts from the Cathedral inside the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades, fighting alongside Commander Renault Mograine.",al={"whitemane lore","who is high inquisitor whitemane","scarlet monastery boss"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Whitemane hate the undead so much?",a="During the Third War, Whitemane's family was infected by the plague of undeath while traveling through northern Lordaeron. She was forced to slay her own parents and siblings once they reanimated as mindless Scourge, scarring her with immense grief and driving her obsessive mission to eradicate all undead.",al={"why does whitemane hate scourge","whitemane backstory","whitemane family"},it="motive"},{q="Where did Whitemane grow up?",a="She grew up in the town of Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills, playing games of monster-slaying alongside childhood friends Renault Mograine and James Vishas long before they joined the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"whitemane childhood","where is whitemane from"},it="origin"},{q="Why does the Alliance want Whitemane dead?",a="Raleigh the Devout, a former Crusader in Southshore, believes the Scarlet Crusade has devolved into paranoia and madness. He asks Alliance champions to eliminate Whitemane and Mograine so the order can potentially return to its honorable origins.",al={"raleigh the devout whitemane","why kill whitemane alliance","in the name of the light quest"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does the Horde want Whitemane dead?",a="Varimathras and the Forsaken in the Undercity view the Scarlet Crusade as an active, hostile presence right outside their capital. The dreadlord orders her death to shatter the Monastery's leadership and remove an immediate threat to the Forsaken realm.",al={"varimathras whitemane quest","into the scarlet monastery","why horde kills whitemane"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Whitemane's relationship with Renault Mograine?",a="Whitemane and Renault Mograine were childhood companions in Southshore who grew into the dual leaders of the Scarlet Monastery. Fighting side by side in the Cathedral, they share an intimate bond and mutual devotion to the Crusade's crusade against undeath.",al={"whitemane and mograine","commander mograine and whitemane"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Sally Whitemane on?",a="Sally Whitemane is a zealous leader of the Scarlet Crusade, serving as their High Inquisitor. She owes no allegiance to the Alliance or the Horde, viewing outsiders with extreme suspicion and fanaticism. Whitemane is fiercely loyal to the Crusade's dogma, fighting alongside Commander Renault Mograine to purge any who stand in their path.",al={"whitemane faction","who does whitemane fight for","whitemane allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Sally Whitemane want?",a="Whitemane desires the utter eradication of the undead. After enduring the horror of seeing her family succumb to the plague and being forced to slay them herself, she was consumed by rage and guilt. She finds purpose only in purging the Scourge and anyone she deems tainted by undeath.",al={"whitemane goals","what does whitemane want","whitemane motivation"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Sally Whitemane here?",a="As High Inquisitor, Sally Whitemane directs the Scarlet Crusade's operations from deep within the Scarlet Monastery's Cathedral. There she oversees the defense of their northern Lordaeron sanctuary, rallying the crusaders and purging all who trespass upon their holy stronghold.",al={"why is whitemane in the monastery","whitemane cathedral why","why is whitemane here"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Why is Sally Whitemane famous or feared?",a="Whitemane is feared for her unyielding fanatical zeal and her formidable mastery of holy magic. As the High Inquisitor of the Scarlet Crusade, she has earned a terrifying reputation for ruthlessly purging suspected corruption and raising fallen allies, including Commander Mograine, in the midst of battle.",al={"why is whitemane feared","whitemane reputation","why is whitemane famous"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["class:Priest"]="Whitemane demonstrates the terrifying power of the Holy Light when fused with unbending zealotry, serving as a cautionary example of how conviction can transform into fanatical ruthlessness.",["class:Paladin"]="To paladins of the Silver Hand, Whitemane's leadership exemplifies the tragic corruption of Lordaeron's defenders, who abandoned mercy and justice in favor of indiscriminate purges.",["race:Undead"]="To the Forsaken, Whitemane embodies the Crusade's refusal to distinguish between mindless Scourge and free-willed undead, making her destruction essential for the survival of the Undercity.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though she was once an Alliance citizen of Lordaeron, Whitemane's Crusade now attacks any outsiders who approach their lands, forcing Southshore's loyalists to confront the monsters their former kin have become."},kw={"cathedral","high inquisitor","raleigh the devout","renault mograine","sally whitemane","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","whitemane"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:southshore","subzone:hearthglen","zone:undercity","npc:varimathras","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Sally Whitemane"}}
E["npc:scarlet-commander-mograine"] = {t="npc",n="Scarlet Commander Mograine",z="scarlet",s="Scarlet Commander Mograine serves as the military leader garrisoned inside the Cathedral of the Scarlet Monastery. A zealous paladin of the Scarlet Crusade, he defends the chapel alongside High Inquisitor Whitemane. Both the Horde and Alliance target him to disrupt the zealots threatening Tirisfal Glades and the surrounding lands.",h="Scarlet Commander Mograine serves as the military leader garrisoned inside the Cathedral of the Scarlet...",sec={{t="Defender of the Chapel",b="Stationed within the grand Crusader's Chapel at the heart of the Scarlet Monastery, Scarlet Commander Mograine commands the standing garrison of the Scarlet Crusade. He wields the holy power of a paladin with ferocious dedication, relying on retribution, divine shields, and stunning blows to shatter any whom the Crusade deems corrupted or unclean.",sp=0},{t="A Miraculous Bond",b="Mograine's defense of the chapel is intrinsically tied to High Inquisitor Whitemane. Should an attacking force bring the Commander to his knees, Whitemane emerges from the rear sanctum to turn the tide. Calling upon the Holy Light, she incapacitates intruders in an instant and restores Mograine from death, forcing their foes to confront both commanders in a desperate, simultaneous struggle.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can Scarlet Commander Mograine be found?",a="He is located inside the Cathedral wing of the Scarlet Monastery in northeastern Tirisfal Glades. You will find him waiting before the altar within the Crusader's Chapel.",al={"mograine location","where is mograine","scarlet monastery mograine room"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Mograine's role in the Scarlet Crusade?",a="He serves as the military commander of the Scarlet Crusade's forces garrisoned at the Monastery, directing its paladins and soldiers alongside High Inquisitor Whitemane.",al={"who is commander mograine","mograine rank","what does mograine do"},it="identity"},{q="How does he fight?",a="Mograine fights as a heavy melee paladin. He uses Hammer of Justice to stun his opponents, unleashes Crusader Strikes, protects himself with Retribution Aura, and relies on Divine Shield when pushed to the brink.",al={"mograine abilities","mograine combat","how to fight mograine"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Why does High Inquisitor Whitemane revive him?",a="Whitemane and Mograine share an intense bond and fight together as leaders of the Monastery. When Mograine falls in battle, Whitemane intervenes, puts their attackers to sleep with her magic, and raises Mograine back to life with full strength.",al={"whitemane res mograine","does mograine revive","resurrect mograine"},it="ties"},{q="Why are the Alliance and Horde fighting him?",a="The Scarlet Crusade views all outsiders—living or undead—as carriers of corruption. Both the Alliance and the Forsaken send champions to strike at the Cathedral and execute its leaders to neutralize the Crusade's fanatical presence in Lordaeron.",al={"why kill mograine","scarlet commander quest","in the name of the light"},it="conflict"},{q="Does Mograine heal himself during the encounter?",a="Yes, in a pinch. Besides Divine Shield and his melee attacks, he can call on Lay on Hands to restore himself to full health, and High Inquisitor Whitemane adds further healing once she enters the battle.",al={"can mograine heal","mograine healing"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Scarlet Commander Mograine on?",a="Commander Mograine fights solely for the Scarlet Crusade. Though once drawn from Lordaeron's surviving defenders and the Knights of the Silver Hand, the Crusade now stands entirely isolated. Under Mograine's military command, they view all outsiders—Horde and Alliance alike—as plague-ridden filth and enemies of the Holy Light.",al={"who does mograine fight for","scarlet commander mograine faction","is mograine alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Scarlet Commander Mograine at the Monastery?",a="The Scarlet Monastery serves as a principal bastion of the Scarlet Crusade in Tirisfal Glades. Mograine holds the Crusader's Chapel within the Cathedral, directing the garrison's military defense alongside High Inquisitor Whitemane while guarding the heart of their holy fortress.",al={"why is mograine in scarlet monastery","mograine location reason","what is mograine doing here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Mograine embodies the tragic corruption of the paladin's calling, twisting holy vows of protection and righteousness into ruthless, unyielding zealotry.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Commander Mograine represents the sharpest blade of the Scarlet Crusade, whose presence directly borders the Undercity and threatens their survival in Tirisfal.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though the Scarlet Crusade once shared common ground with the Alliance, leaders in Southshore and Stormwind recognize that fanatical commanders like Mograine have descended into violent madness."},kw={"cathedral","crusader's chapel","mograine","paladin","scarlet commander mograine","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","whitemane"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:light"},src={"Scarlet Commander Mograine"}}
E["subzone:chamber-of-atonement"] = {t="subzone",n="Chamber of Atonement",z="scarlet",s="The Chamber of Atonement is the grim entrance hall to the Graveyard wing within the Scarlet Monastery. Here, beneath stone arches hung with iron chains, the Scarlet Crusade subjects captured undead and other perceived heretics to brutal interrogation and torture before casting their remains into the cloister beyond.",h="The Chamber of Atonement is the grim entrance hall to the Graveyard wing within the Scarlet Monastery.",sec={{t="A Hall of Agony",b="Serving as the threshold to the Forlorn Cloister, the Chamber of Atonement is far from a sanctuary of peaceful prayer. Instead, the Scarlet Crusade has converted the grand entryway into a house of pain, outfitted with racks, shackles, and burning braziers. Zealous inquisitors use these instruments to extract confessions and torment captives, viewing excruciating pain as the only fitting penance for unholy beings. The chamber echoes constantly with the cries of the damned, presided over by cruel taskmasters who ensure that those who enter rarely walk out whole.",sp=0},{t="The Interrogator's Domain",b="The chamber is overseen by Interrogator Vishas, one of the Crusade's most sadistic practitioners of coercion. Vishas takes grotesque pride in breaking the resolve of anyone caught crossing the monastery's boundaries. Among his prized victims is the Forsaken captive Vorrel Sengutz, who has endured endless weeks of torment at Vishas's hands. The cruelty practiced within these walls proves to outsiders that the Scarlet Crusade's crusade for purity has twisted into wanton sadism.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Chamber of Atonement used for?",a="It serves as the interrogation and torture wing for the Scarlet Crusade inside the Graveyard wing of the monastery. Captives, primarily Forsaken and other perceived enemies, are questioned, broken, and tortured here using brutal implements before their bodies are cast out into the graveyard.",al={"chamber purpose","why are there torture devices here","what happens in chamber of atonement"},it="purpose"},{q="Who controls this chamber?",a="The room is under the command of Interrogator Vishas, a sadistic torturer of the Scarlet Crusade notorious for deriving pleasure from his victims' suffering.",al={"who is the boss here","chamber of atonement leader","who runs the torture chamber"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where does this room lead?",a="It is the outermost hall of the Graveyard wing and leads directly into the Forlorn Cloister, the open-air cemetery grounds where fallen Crusaders and restless dead reside.",al={"chamber exits","where does chamber of atonement go","next area after atonement"},it="place"},{q="Who is being held captive here?",a="A Forsaken captive named Vorrel Sengutz has been imprisoned and tortured in the chamber by Interrogator Vishas for weeks on end.",al={"who is prisoner here","vorrel sengutz","tortured prisoner"},it="target"},{q="What is the Chamber of Atonement?",a="The Chamber of Atonement is the outermost hall of the Graveyard wing within the Scarlet Monastery. Positioned directly before the Forlorn Cloister and the open cemetery grounds, it serves as a grim threshold where the Scarlet Crusade drags captives to endure brutal interrogations.",al={"what is chamber of atonement","chamber of atonement info","about chamber of atonement"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is the Chamber of Atonement dangerous?",a="It is exceedingly dangerous. The chamber is manned by fanatical Scarlet torturers led by Interrogator Vishas, surrounded by gruesome implements of torment. Any intruders or perceived sympathizers of the undead are immediately set upon and subjected to the same merciless cruelty visited upon their prisoners.",al={"is chamber of atonement dangerous","chamber of atonement threats","how dangerous is chamber of atonement"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Chamber of Atonement?",a="The Scarlet Crusade named the hall for their twisted belief that any being tainted by undeath or opposing their crusade must confess and pay for their sins through agony. To the inquisitors, suffering and torture under their blades are the only true paths to penance.",al={"why chamber of atonement","chamber of atonement name meaning","why is it called atonement"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Chamber of Atonement represents the height of Scarlet cruelty toward your people, serving as the site where captive Forsaken like Vorrel Sengutz are systematically tortured for existing.",["class:Priest"]="The desecration of holy vows is nowhere more evident than here, where Crusade interrogators twist sacred discipline into physical butchery and sadistic torment."},kw={"chamber of atonement","forlorn cloister","graveyard","interrogator vishas","scarlet monastery","torture","vorrel sengutz"},rel={"zone:scarlet","npc:interrogator-vishas","subzone:forlorn-cloister","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:forsaken"},src={"Chamber of Atonement"}}
E["subzone:crusader-s-armory"] = {t="subzone",n="Crusader's Armory",z="scarlet",s="The Crusader's Armory is a fortified interior hall within the Scarlet Monastery Armory wing. Stockpiled with munitions, gunpowder, and cannonballs, it serves as a staging ground for the zealots guarding the path toward the inner sanctum. Beyond its locked iron door lies the Hall of Champions.",h="The Crusader's Armory is a fortified interior hall within the Scarlet Monastery Armory wing.",sec={{t="Arsenal of Zeal",b="Situated between the Footman's Armory and the grand Hall of Champions, the Crusader's Armory displays the full military readiness of the Scarlet Crusade. Unlike the training yards outside, these narrow stone corridors are packed to the ceiling with crates of volatile gunpowder, stacked cannonballs, and heavily armed crusaders ready to repel intruders. The Crusade has turned a former monastic compound into a bristling fortress, dedicating every available hall to the tools of total war. At the far end of the armory stands a heavy locked iron door, barring entry to the inner chambers unless one holds the Scarlet Key.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Crusader's Armory?",a="The Crusader's Armory is an interior section of the Scarlet Monastery's Armory wing. It acts as an ammunition depot and defensive corridor between the Footman's Armory and the Hall of Champions.",al={"crusaders armory","what is crusaders armory","monastery armory room"},it="place"},{q="Why is the door at the end locked?",a="The door at the end of the Crusader's Armory guards the passage into the Hall of Champions and the commander's quarters beyond. The Scarlet Crusade keeps it strictly secured, requiring the Scarlet Key found in the Monastery's Library wing to unlock it.",al={"locked door armory","how to open armory door","scarlet key armory"},gp=true},{q="Why are there so many cannonballs and gunpowder crates here?",a="The Scarlet Crusade maintains an active siege presence and artillery defenses across Tirisfal Glades. This armory acts as a central storage magazine for their cannons and explosive ordnance, ensuring their troops remain well-supplied for war against the Scourge and Forsaken.",al={"powder crates armory","cannons in monastery","why gunpowder"},it="purpose"},{q="Who guards this area?",a="The hall is defended by seasoned Scarlet Crusade soldiers, including footmen, crusaders, and archers stationed among the munitions to stop any invaders trying to penetrate deeper into the complex.",al={"armory mobs","who is in crusaders armory"},it="residents"},{q="Is the Crusader's Armory dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The armory is packed with zealous Scarlet Crusade fighters who attack any intruder on sight, treating every outsider as an agent of corruption or the Scourge. Adding to the peril, the entire corridor is crammed with high explosives, including volatile powder kegs and artillery stockpiles ready for their relentless war in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"crusaders armory danger","is crusaders armory safe","crusader armory threats"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Crusader's Armory?",a="The chamber takes its name from the Scarlet Crusaders who garrison it and store their siege materiel within. Situated deep within the Scarlet Monastery's military wing past the Footman's Armory, it holds the cannon shot, gunpowder, and weapons designated for the Crusade's seasoned warriors as they prepare to assault the surrounding Plaguelands.",al={"why is it called crusaders armory","crusaders armory name origin","crusader armory meaning"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Forsaken and Horde, the explosive stores in the Crusader's Armory represent a direct threat to the borders of Tirisfal Glades and the gates of the Undercity.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="The arms and munitions stockpiled here demonstrate the high production value and military discipline of Lordaeron's former smiths, now turned to zealous fanaticism."},kw={"armory","crusader's armory","gunpowder","hall of champions","scarlet key","scarlet monastery"},rel={"subzone:scarlet-monastery-armory","subzone:hall-of-champions","zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Crusader's Armory"}}
E["subzone:forlorn-cloister"] = {t="subzone",n="Forlorn Cloister",z="scarlet",s="The Forlorn Cloister is the haunted graveyard wing of the Scarlet Monastery. Here, members of the Scarlet Crusade desperately torch the bodies of fallen brothers to prevent them from rising into undeath, while restless spirits and shambling corpses roam among the tombs.",h="The Forlorn Cloister is the haunted graveyard wing of the Scarlet Monastery.",sec={{t="A Consecration Consumed",b="Once a peaceful sanctuary where the priests and paladins of Lordaeron laid their honoured dead to rest, the Forlorn Cloister has become a grim charnel ground. Despite the Scarlet Crusade's fanatical vigilance, the taint of the plague has seeped deep into the earth. crusaders patrol the fog-shrouded cemetery with torches, frantically burning remains to stave off the rot. Even so, spectres glide between crypts and the dead pull free from their graves, ruled over by dark magic deep within the grounds.",sp=0},{t="The Master of the Tombs",b="Deep within the cloister lurks Bloodmage Thalnos, a sadistic Scarlet torturer whose horrific fate embodies the tragedy of the Monastery. Risen as a skeletal horror after contracting the plague, Thalnos has embraced dark necromancy, binding the souls of the deceased and slaughtering any who dare intrude upon his blighted graveyard.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Forlorn Cloister located?",a="The Forlorn Cloister makes up the outdoor graveyard wing of the Scarlet Monastery, situated in the northeastern corner of Tirisfal Glades.",al={"forlorn cloister location","where is cloister","graveyard wing"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the Scarlet Crusaders burning bodies here?",a="The Crusade burns the dead in a desperate attempt to keep the Scourge plague from animating their fallen comrades. Because the soil of the cloister is already tainted, unburned bodies swiftly rise as mindless zombies.",al={"why burn corpses","burning bodies scarlet","what are crusaders doing"},it="purpose"},{q="Who rules over the Forlorn Cloister?",a="The graveyard is dominated by Bloodmage Thalnos, a powerful undead spellcaster who commands the wandering dead and attacks any living intruders.",al={"cloister boss","who is in charge here","graveyard boss"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is the graveyard haunted if the Scarlet Crusade holds the Monastery?",a="Despite their religious fervour, the Crusaders have lost control of their own cemetery. The relentless necromantic energies sweeping through Lordaeron have stirred the buried dead, leaving the living garrison trapped in a ceaseless battle against the spirits of their former peers.",al={"why are there ghosts","why undead in monastery","is graveyard scourge"}},{q="What is the Forlorn Cloister?",a="The Forlorn Cloister is the open-air graveyard wing of the Scarlet Monastery. Once a peaceful place of rest for the order's fallen, it has deteriorated into a desolate courtyard where earth and crypts crawl with restless dead. Even as the Scarlet Crusade fiercely defends the rest of the monastery, here they fight a desperate, unending skirmish simply to contain the horrors rising from the soil.",al={"what is forlorn cloister","forlorn cloister scarlet monastery","about forlorn cloister"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is the Forlorn Cloister dangerous?",a="Extremely dangerous. You face a deadly crossfire between zealous Scarlet Crusaders and the shambling dead they cannot control. Lingering spirits, restless wraiths, and walking corpses wander among the tombstones, while crusaders aggressively purge anyone who interferes. Deeper within dwells Thalnos the Soulrender, a fallen mage of devastating power who tears into the souls of any who intrude upon his domain.",al={"is forlorn cloister dangerous","forlorn cloister threats","danger in forlorn cloister"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["class:Priest"]="Walking the Forlorn Cloister is a sobering reminder of what happens when holy sanctums fall to darkness, as holy rites give way to frantic pyres and tortured apparitions.",["race:Undead"]="The Forsaken observe a grim irony in the cloister: the zealous Crusaders who brand all undead as monsters cannot even stop their own brothers from rising beneath their feet."},kw={"forlorn cloister","graveyard","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","soulrender","thalnos","tirisfal glades"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Forlorn Cloister"}}
E["subzone:gallery-of-treasures"] = {t="subzone",n="Gallery of Treasures",z="scarlet",s="The Gallery of Treasures is an ornate, heavily guarded corridor inside the Scarlet Monastery's halls, connecting the Huntsman's Cloister to the Athenaeum. Lined with recovered paintings, relics, and illuminated texts, it showcases the wealth and Lordaeron heritage preserved by the Scarlet Crusade amidst their zealous war against the undead.",h="The Gallery of Treasures is an ornate, heavily guarded corridor inside the Scarlet Monastery's halls...",sec={{t="A Repository of Lost Heritage",b="Situated deep within the Library wing of the Scarlet Monastery, the Gallery of Treasures serves as a grand hall connecting the kennels of the Huntsman's Cloister to the sacred archives of the Athenaeum. Unlike the hound pens of the cloister, this corridor is lined with fine paintings, historical artifacts, and small chambers filled with books salvaged from across the fallen kingdom of Lordaeron. To the Scarlet Crusade, these relics represent the untainted legacy of humanity they have sworn to protect, fiercely guarded against all outsiders who dare intrude upon their sanctuary.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Gallery of Treasures located?",a="It is located inside the Library wing of the Scarlet Monastery. The gallery sits directly past the Huntsman's Cloister and serves as the final decorated passageway before reaching the Athenaeum.",al={"gallery location","where is gallery of treasures","how to find gallery of treasures"},it="place"},{q="What is kept in the Gallery of Treasures?",a="The gallery houses preserved artwork, historical relics, illuminated texts, and paintings salvaged from the ruined kingdom of Lordaeron, displayed along the corridor and in adjoining reading chambers.",al={"what is in gallery of treasures","gallery loot","gallery relics"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does the Scarlet Crusade collect these treasures?",a="The Scarlet Crusade views itself as the true remnant of Lordaeron. Salvaging and hoarding these cultural works allows them to preserve the memory and sacred heritage of their homeland while purging the lands of what they see as taint.",al={"why do scarlet have treasures","crusade relics purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Who guards the gallery?",a="The corridor is patrolled by various zealots of the Scarlet Crusade, including defenders and initiates who guard the path leading toward Arcanist Doan and the monastery's deeper archives.",al={"gallery mobs","who is in gallery of treasures"},it="residents"},{q="Is the Gallery of Treasures dangerous?",a="Yes, deeply so. The gallery is heavily guarded by zealous Scarlet Crusade defenders who view any outsider as an agent of corruption or the Scourge. Navigating its ornate halls means fighting past disciplined crusaders ready to slaughter trespassers on sight.",al={"is gallery of treasures dangerous","gallery of treasures danger","scarlet monastery gallery danger"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The artifacts and banners lining this gallery reflect the lost glory of the Silver Hand and fallen Lordaeron, though now held by zealots who have turned righteous conviction into indiscriminate fanaticism.",["race:Undead"]="The paintings and historical heirlooms preserved here belonged to the ancestors of the Forsaken, jealously guarded by living crusaders who seek to wipe out the former citizens of Lordaeron."},kw={"athenaeum","gallery of treasures","library","lordaeron relics","paintings","scarlet halls","scarlet monastery"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Gallery of Treasures"}}
E["subzone:grand-vestibule"] = {t="subzone",n="Grand Vestibule",z="scarlet",s="The Grand Vestibule is the monumental entrance hall of the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades. Lined with crimson pillars and stone effigies of fallen crusaders, it serves as the threshold where adventurers prepare to breach the monastery's inner halls.",h="The Grand Vestibule is the monumental entrance hall of the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="The Threshold of Zealotry",b="Past the heavy outer gates of the Monastery lies the Grand Vestibule, an expansive marble hall dedicated to the martial pride of the Scarlet Crusade. Statues of armored champions stand vigil beside vaulted stone pillars, and zealous sentries, disciples, and augurs patrol the flagstones to strike down anyone daring to enter without the order's crimson tabard. For trespassers, it is the first taste of the Crusade's unrelenting discipline and fanaticism.",sp=0},{t="A Contested Meeting Ground",b="Because the vestibule sits directly outside the secured inner wings of the monastery, it functions as a perilous gathering point. Both Alliance strike teams sent north and Horde forces pushing out from the nearby Undercity converge under these high arches, turning the ornate entry into a chaotic and bloody battleground long before anyone breaches the inner cloisters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Grand Vestibule?",a="It is the grand entrance chamber of the Scarlet Monastery in northeastern Tirisfal Glades, connecting the outer courtyard to the four interior wings.",al={"what is this room","grand vestibule info","monastery entrance hall"},it="place"},{q="What enemies guard this area?",a="The chamber is defended by active Scarlet Crusade personnel, primarily Scarlet Sentries, Scarlet Disciples, and Scarlet Augurs stationed to bar intruders.",al={"who patrols here","vestibule mobs","crusaders in vestibule"},it="threat"},{q="Why do the Alliance and Horde fight here?",a="Both factions send champions into the Monastery—the Alliance seeking to reclaim Lordaeron's holy sites or purge heretics, and the Horde acting to secure Tirisfal Glades for the Forsaken. Their paths inevitably collide in this shared entrance hall.",al={"pvp in vestibule","why are players fighting here","contested vestibule"},it="conflict"},{q="Whom do the statues in the vestibule depict?",a="The statues depict honored warriors and heroes of the Scarlet Crusade, sculpted in heavy plate armor to serve as enduring symbols of their unyielding crusade against the undead.",al={"who are the statues","vestibule statues","crusade monuments"}},{q="Who controls the Grand Vestibule?",a="The Scarlet Crusade holds total dominion over this grand entry chamber. Scarlet Augurs, Disciples, and Sentries stand watch among the towering pillars and carved statues, fiercely guarding the threshold to their inner sanctums against any whom they deem tainted or unworthy.",al={"who lives in grand vestibule","who runs grand vestibule","grand vestibule control"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is the Grand Vestibule dangerous?",a="Extremely so. Beyond the vigilant Scarlet Crusade defenders posted throughout the hall, the vestibule is a frequent flashpoint between Alliance and Horde adventurers seeking entry into the monastery's wings, leading to sudden and bloody skirmishes right at the doorstep.",al={"is grand vestibule safe","how dangerous is grand vestibule","grand vestibule danger"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is this hall called the Grand Vestibule?",a="A vestibule serves as an entrance hall or antechamber leading into a larger structure. As the outermost chamber of the Scarlet Monastery, its expansive architecture, towering colonnades, and ornate statues of crusade heroes make it truly grand in scale and purpose.",al={"why grand vestibule","grand vestibule name origin","meaning of grand vestibule"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Positioned just northeast of the Undercity, this grand entryway represents the frontline of the living zealots actively threatening Forsaken sovereignty in Tirisfal.",["faction:Alliance"]="The vestibule displays the tragic corruption of Lordaeron's former holy sanctuaries, showing how devotion to the Light curdled into blind, violent fanaticism."},kw={"entrance hall","grand vestibule","scarlet augur","scarlet disciple","scarlet monastery","scarlet sentry","tirisfal glades"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Grand Vestibule"}}
E["subzone:hall-of-champions"] = {t="subzone",n="Hall of Champions",z="scarlet",s="The Hall of Champions is an honored gallery nestled deep within the training grounds of the Scarlet Monastery. Lined with statues of fallen heroes, it serves as a solemn memorial to legendary crusaders and a proving ground for the Scarlet Crusade's elite.",h="The Hall of Champions is an honored gallery nestled deep within the training grounds of the Scarlet Monastery.",sec={{t="A Memorial to the Fallen",b="Situated past the Footman's Armory, the Hall of Champions stands as a testament to the storied figures who shaped the Scarlet Crusade's holy war. Stone memorials line the walls, depicting honored heroes such as Admiral Barean Westwind, Harthal Truesight, and Holia Sunshield. Here, amidst the frozen gazes of their greatest warriors, Scarlet trainees draw inspiration, hardening their resolve to purge Lordaeron of all undead and outsiders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Hall of Champions?",a="The hall serves as a memorial gallery dedicated to celebrated champions of the Scarlet Crusade. Its walls are lined with statues honoring prominent figures such as Barean Westwind, Invar One-Arm, and Harthal Truesight, reminding crusaders of their martial heritage.",al={"what is hall of champions","hall of champions purpose","why are there statues here"},it="purpose"},{q="Who are the people immortalized in the statues?",a="The statues depict fallen and venerated veterans of the Crusade, including High Elf and human commanders such as Arellas Fireleaf, Fellari Swiftarrow, Holia Sunshield, Ferren Marcus, Orman of Stromgarde, and Dorgar Stoenbrow.",al={"who are the statues","statue names hall of champions","monastery statues"},it="people"},{q="How does this hall differ from Stormwind's Champions' Hall?",a="Despite the similar name, this chamber is located deep inside the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades, dedicated strictly to Scarlet martyrs. Stormwind City's Champions' Hall is a military garrison reserved for Alliance officers and PvP quartermasters.",al={"is this stormwind pvp hall","hall of champions vs champions hall","pvp hall confusion"}},{q="What is the Hall of Champions?",a="The Hall of Champions is a dedicated memorial chamber situated within the Scarlet Monastery's halls, just beyond the Footman's Armory. It serves as a revered gallery lined with stone statues commemorating notable figures, commanders, and fallen heroes of the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"what is hall of champions","hall of champions scarlet"},it="place",add=true},{q="Who oversees the Hall of Champions?",a="The chamber is overseen by Armsmaster Harlan, the weapons trainer of the Scarlet Crusade. He occupies the hall to drill crusaders in martial prowess beneath the watchful stone eyes of the order's greatest historical champions.",al={"who runs hall of champions","who is in hall of champions","hall of champions boss"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is the Hall of Champions dangerous?",a="Yes, it is extremely dangerous. The Scarlet Crusade regards all outsiders as plague-ridden enemies or heretics to be purged on sight. Armsmaster Harlan and the zealous defenders stationed throughout these grounds will attack any trespasser without hesitation.",al={"is hall of champions safe","danger hall of champions"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Hall of Champions?",a="The chamber takes its name from the memorial statues lining its walls, each carved in tribute to past champions, knights, and commanders of the Scarlet Crusade whose deeds the order seeks to honor and emulate.",al={"why called hall of champions","name hall of champions"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For knights of the Holy Light, looking upon the honored statues of figures like Harthal Truesight is a somber reminder of how genuine virtue and faith can become twisted by zealotry.",["race:Human"]="Human travelers from Lordaeron and Stromgarde may recognize the names carved into the plinths, noting former defenders of the northern kingdoms who threw their lot in with the fanatical Crusade."},kw={"barean westwind","footman's armory","hall of champions","harthal truesight","holia sunshield","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","statues"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:champions-hall","subzone:hall-of-legends"},src={"Hall of Champions"}}
E["subzone:room-of-hidden-secrets"] = {t="subzone",n="Room of Hidden Secrets",z="scarlet",s="The Room of Hidden Secrets is a quiet interior chamber tucked within the Scarlet Monastery's armory wing, situated between the Hall of Champions and the Gallery of Treasures. Despite its enigmatic and solemn name, any profound lore or hidden arcane mysteries within its walls remain an elusive curiosity to the zealots stationed nearby.",h="The Room of Hidden Secrets is a quiet interior chamber tucked within the Scarlet Monastery's armory wing...",sec={{t="An Unassuming Sanctuary",b="Located in the fortified passages leading toward the armory's innermost treasury, the Room of Hidden Secrets appears to be little more than another stone-walled chamber built during the monastery's expansion. Positioned directly beyond the Hall of Champions and just before the Gallery of Treasures, it sits within the heavily guarded bastion of the Scarlet Crusade. While its grand title implies concealed relics or classified Crusade doctrines, the Crusaders themselves pay little attention to whatever mundane or supernatural oddities linger unseen in the corners.",sp=0},{t="Unseen Inhabitants",b="Those gifted with supernatural perception or specialized sensory aids claim the room harbors an entirely different kind of mystery. Wandering unseen across the cold flagstones are phantasmal rodents, known to observers as Sekret and Sekrit. These ghostly critters are completely invisible to ordinary mortal eyes, slipping silently beneath the notice of the fanatical guards marching through the halls.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Room of Hidden Secrets located?",a="It is located inside the Armory wing of the Scarlet Monastery. You pass through it after clearing the Hall of Champions and immediately before stepping into the Gallery of Treasures.",al={"room of hidden secrets location","where is room of hidden secrets","scarlet monastery secrets room"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is actually hidden in this room?",a="Rather than forbidden Crusade records or holy relics, the only hidden presences detected within the room are a pair of ethereal phantom rodents named Sekret and Sekrit, which remain invisible to the naked eye.",al={"what secrets are in the room","what is hidden here","room secrets"},it="purpose"},{q="How can you see the spirits in this chamber?",a="The spectral rodents cannot be viewed by normal vision. They can only be revealed through the keen senses granted by specialized detection abilities used by rogues or through the technological optics of an Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer.",al={"how to see ghost rats","see sekrit","detect ghosts scarlet monastery"},gp=true},{q="Does the Scarlet Crusade know about the room's secret?",a="There is no indication the Crusade is aware of the ghostly rodents. The zealots are entirely preoccupied with their paranoid holy war against the undead, leaving the minor spectral quirks of their monastery unnoticed.",al={"do scarlet crusade know","crusade lore on secrets room"}},{q="What is the Room of Hidden Secrets?",a="The Room of Hidden Secrets is a small chamber located inside the Scarlet Monastery's halls, situated along the corridor between the Hall of Champions and the Gallery of Treasures. Despite its grand and mysterious name, it functions mainly as a connecting passageway within the fortified complex.",al={"what is room of hidden secrets","room of hidden secrets purpose","scarlet halls hidden room"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is the Room of Hidden Secrets dangerous?",a="Any danger in the room comes from the Scarlet Crusade zealots patrolling the nearby halls. The chamber itself conceals only the unseen, harmless apparitions of two spectral rodents named Sekret and Sekrit, which pose no direct physical threat to anyone passing through.",al={"room of hidden secrets safe","is room of hidden secrets dangerous","monastery room dangers"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Room of Hidden Secrets?",a="The chamber earns its curious moniker from the pair of ethereal rodents, Sekret and Sekrit, hidden within its walls. Because these spirits remain invisible to ordinary sight without specialized tools or keen senses, the room's modest secrets stay hidden in plain view.",al={"why is it called room of hidden secrets","room of hidden secrets name origin","why room of hidden secrets"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Rogues with sharp senses can utilize their Detection abilities to spot the otherwise invisible phantom rats roaming the stone floors.",["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers equipped with an Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer can pierce the veil to glimpse the ethereal creatures hiding in plain sight."},kw={"armory","detection","ghost rats","room of hidden secrets","scarlet monastery","sekret","sekrit"},rel={"subzone:gallery-of-treasures","subzone:hall-of-champions","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:scarlet"},src={"Room of Hidden Secrets"}}
E["subzone:scarlet-monastery-armory"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarlet Monastery Armory",z="scarlet",s="The Armory is the fortified martial wing of the Scarlet Monastery, dedicated to manufacturing weapons and training recruits for the Scarlet Crusade. Behind locked iron gates, ranks of zealous footmen and crusaders drill under the fierce command of Herod, the Scarlet Champion.",h="The Armory is the fortified martial wing of the Scarlet Monastery, dedicated to manufacturing weapons and...",sec={{t="The Foundry of Zeal",b="Once part of a peaceful retreat for Lordaeron's priesthood, the monastery was completely overhauled following the Third War. The Armory now serves as the Crusade's primary forge, weapons depot, and combat proving ground. From the open training grounds to the deep weapon halls, ranks of Scarlet footmen, conjurers, and crusaders prepare relentlessly to purge the Scourge and anyone else they deem tainted. The wing remains locked away from the Grand Vestibule, accessible only to those carrying the Scarlet Key found in the neighboring Library.",sp=0},{t="The Hall of Champions",b="At the heart of the wing lies the Hall of Champions, lined with towering statues dedicated to legendary heroes of the Crusade's past. The hall is overseen by Herod, a brutal warrior whose ferocity and whirlwinds are legendary among the crusaders. Herod trains the next generation of zealots personally; when hard-pressed in battle, his desperate recruits will pour into the chamber to fight and die for their champion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you get inside the Armory?",a="The Armory door in the Grand Vestibule is securely locked. To open it, you must enter the Library wing and retrieve the Scarlet Key from the chest behind Arcanist Doan in the Athenaeum, or bring a rogue proficient enough in lockpicking.",al={"armory locked","how to unlock armory","scarlet key armory","open armory door"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Who leads the troops in the Armory?",a="The wing is commanded by Herod, known as the Scarlet Champion. Stationed within the Hall of Champions, he drills soldiers and puts incoming recruits through intense combat trials.",al={"armory boss","who is in charge of armory","who runs the armory","herod armory"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the purpose of this wing for the Scarlet Crusade?",a="It serves as the Crusade's main arsenal and training academy. The complex houses extensive weapon forges, armories for footmen and crusaders, and outdoor drilling yards used to condition soldiers before dispatching them across Tirisfal and the Plaguelands.",al={"why does armory exist","what do they do here","armory purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose statues are honored in the Hall of Champions?",a="The statues celebrate the order's most praised martyrs and heroes, including early fighters and champions like Barean Westwind, Orman of Stromgarde, and Ferren Marcus.",al={"armory statues","hall of champions statues","statues in herod room"},it="fame"},{q="What is the Scarlet Monastery Armory?",a="The Armory is a heavily fortified wing within the Scarlet Monastery complex in Tirisfal Glades. Once dedicated to the peaceful worship and study of the Holy Light under Lordaeron's priesthood, it now serves as the training barracks, weapons depot, and assembly grounds for the Scarlet Crusade's militant zealots.",al={"what is the armory","scarlet monastery armory lore","about armory"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened to the Armory?",a="During the Third War, the Scourge decimated Lordaeron, sweeping through the region and transforming the peaceful center of learning into a desperate redoubt. Surviving clergy and soldiers radicalized into the Scarlet Crusade, arming themselves and fortifying the grounds into an unyielding bastion committed to exterminating anyone they suspect of harboring the plague.",al={"armory history","what happened at the armory","scarlet monastery armory background"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is the Armory dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The halls teem with fanatical crusaders, footmen, and battle-mages trained to kill on sight. The Crusade considers all outsiders potential carriers of the Scourge, meaning any intruder who enters the training grounds or halls faces disciplined, relentless soldiers fighting to the death.",al={"how dangerous is the armory","is armory safe","armory threat"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="The Armory is the quintessential proving ground of mortal combat, where Scarlet warriors demonstrate lethal use of stances, disarms, and Herod's renowned whirlwind technique.",["faction:Horde"]="With the Scarlet Crusade massing an army directly outside the gates of the Undercity, raiding their armaments and slaughtering their champion is vital for the Forsaken's survival."},kw={"armory","crusader's armory","footman's armory","hall of champions","herod","scarlet champion","scarlet key","scarlet monastery armory"},rel={"zone:scarlet","npc:herod","subzone:hall-of-champions","subzone:crusader-s-armory","subzone:grand-vestibule","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Scarlet Monastery Armory"}}
E["subzone:scarlet-monastery-cathedral"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarlet Monastery Cathedral",z="scarlet",s="The Cathedral is the spiritual and military heart of the Scarlet Monastery, housing the Crusade's inner sanctum. Once a serene hall of worship for Lordaeron's priesthood, it now serves as the command seat for High Inquisitor Whitemane and Scarlet Commander Mograine, guarded by the Crusade's most devoted zealots.",h="The Cathedral is the spiritual and military heart of the Scarlet Monastery, housing the Crusade's inner...",sec={{t="Sanctum of Zeal",b="Once a peaceful center of enlightenment and prayer for the priesthood of Lordaeron, the Cathedral fell into madness in the wake of the Third War. Following the fall of the kingdom to the Scourge, surviving zealots transformed the complex into a fortress of unyielding hatred. Beyond the manicured cloister of the Chapel Gardens lies the grand Crusader's Chapel, where priests and warriors gather in devotion to their crusade. They view all outsiders—regardless of race or faction—as carriers of the undead plague who must be cleansed by blade and holy fire.",sp=0},{t="The High Inquisitor and Her Commander",b="The forces stationed within the Cathedral answer directly to Scarlet Commander Mograine, who directs the garrison with iron discipline. Yet the true heart of the enclave's fanaticism is High Inquisitor Whitemane. A formidable wielder of the Light, Whitemane's divine devotion enables her to resurrect fallen champions in the heat of battle. Together, she and Mograine hold the inner chapel against any who dare breach the monastery gates, proving that the Crusade's grip on northern Lordaeron remains lethally intact.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Cathedral used for?",a="It serves as the inner redoubt and sacred high seat of the Scarlet Crusade within the Monastery. Here, the organization's highest leaders conduct religious services and direct their military campaigns across Tirisfal Glades.",al={"cathedral purpose","why visit cathedral","what is this place"},it="purpose"},{q="Who leads the Scarlet Crusade here?",a="The garrison is commanded by Scarlet Commander Mograine, while the spiritual authority belongs to High Inquisitor Whitemane, a zealous priestess renowned for her fearsome ability to restore the dead to life.",al={"who is the boss here","cathedral bosses","whitemane mograine"},it="leader"},{q="Why is the door to the Cathedral locked?",a="The heavy gates into the Cathedral wing are locked to keep intruders from storming the inner sanctum. Entering requires the Scarlet Key, which is guarded inside the Monastery's Library wing.",al={"cathedral locked","how to open cathedral","where is the key"},gp=true},{q="Why are the Crusaders attacking other living humans?",a="Driven to paranoid madness by the Scourge's destruction of Lordaeron, the Crusade believes that all outsiders are carriers of the plague of undeath. They refuse contact with external factions and execute anyone who approaches their fortresses.",al={"why attack alliance","scarlet crusade evil","why crusade hostile"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Scarlet Monastery Cathedral?",a="The Cathedral is the central, crowning wing of the Scarlet Monastery complex in Tirisfal Glades. Once a revered sanctuary of Lordaeron's priesthood dedicated to learning and spiritual enlightenment, it now serves as the sanctum sanctorum and command seat for the zealots of the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"what is cathedral","scarlet cathedral","cathedral wing"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened to the Scarlet Monastery Cathedral?",a="Before the Third War, this peaceful monastery stood as a proud bastion of Lordaeron's Holy Light, devoted to study and healing. When the Scourge tore through the kingdom, surviving defenders fortified the holy site, transforming its tranquil halls and courtyards into a heavily armed fortress driven by paranoia and fanatical hatred.",al={"cathedral history","what happened here","monastery past"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is the Scarlet Monastery Cathedral dangerous?",a="It is by far the most perilous quarter of the monastery. Beyond its courtyard lies a grand chapel crammed with elite crusaders, devoted abbots, and deadly sorcerers. Its defenders fight with zealous fury, and intruders face the combined might of Commander Mograine and the formidable High Inquisitor Whitemane.",al={"cathedral danger","is it safe here","how dangerous is cathedral"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the Crusade represents a tragic, corrupt perversion of the Holy Light and Lordaeron's proud heritage, prompting commanders in Southshore to dispatch champions to end their madness.",["faction:Horde"]="Perched dangerously close to the Undercity, the Cathedral houses zealots dedicated to the utter extermination of the Forsaken and any Horde allies who stand with them."},kw={"cathedral","chapel gardens","crusader's chapel","high inquisitor","mograine","scarlet monastery","whitemane"},rel={"zone:scarlet","npc:scarlet-commander-mograine","subzone:grand-vestibule","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:lordaeron","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge","topic:light"},src={"Scarlet Monastery Cathedral"}}
E["subzone:scarlet-monastery-graveyard"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarlet Monastery Graveyard",z="scarlet",s="The Scarlet Monastery Graveyard is the burial wing of the grand religious complex in northeastern Tirisfal Glades. Once a serene resting place for Lordaeron's clergy and nobility, it has fallen into chilling neglect, overrun by lingering undead and the corrupted magic of the fallen crusader Bloodmage Thalnos.",h="The Scarlet Monastery Graveyard is the burial wing of the grand religious complex in northeastern Tirisfal...",sec={{t="A Defiled Sanctuary",b="Before the Third War, this cloistered cemetery served as the peaceful burial ground for the priesthood of Lordaeron. When the Scarlet Crusade fortified the monastery against the undead, their fanatical vigilance failed to cleanse their own crypts. Today, the Graveyard is neglected and deeply haunted. Lingering spirits, restless corpses, and shambling horrors wander the Chamber of Atonement and the mist-covered Forlorn Cloister. Rather than hallowed rest, the dead have found endless torment beneath the crusade's uncaring gaze.",sp=0},{t="Corruption from Within",b="At the rear of the grounds stands Honor's Tomb, where the greatest mockery of the Crusade's dogma festers: Bloodmage Thalnos. Once a sworn defender of the Order, Thalnos succumbed to dark magics and madness, twisted into an undead abomination wielding sinister soul drain and fire. The crusaders above preach total extermination of the undead plague, yet they harbor a rotting, fallen sorcerer within their own consecrated soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there undead inside a Scarlet Crusade stronghold?",a="The Crusade's leadership is consumed with fanaticism, directing their crusaders outward to slaughter living outsiders and wage war in Tirisfal. Consequently, the monastery's crypts and burial plots have been utterly neglected, allowing dormant plague remnants and restless spirits of dead clergy to rise unchecked.",al={"why undead in sm gy","undead in scarlet monastery","why are there ghosts here"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Bloodmage Thalnos?",a="Thalnos was once a mage aligned with the Scarlet Crusade who pursued dark, forbidden magic to fight the Scourge. Instead of purging the undead, his obsession corrupted him into an undead abomination who now rules the desecrated crypts of Honor's Tomb.",al={"thalnos lore","who is bloodmage thalnos","graveyard boss"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Graveyard wing located inside the monastery?",a="Upon entering the Grand Vestibule of the Scarlet Monastery, the Graveyard entrance is the leftmost instance portal. It does not require a key to enter, unlike the Armory and Cathedral wings.",al={"where is sm gy","how to find graveyard wing","which door is graveyard"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Forlorn Cloister?",a="The Forlorn Cloister is the open-air garden and cemetery between the entrance crypts and Honor's Tomb. It is littered with tombstones, roaming ghouls, and damp earth rich in Grave Moss.",al={"forlorn cloister","graveyard courtyard"},it="place"},{q="What is the Scarlet Monastery Graveyard?",a="It is the leftmost wing of the Scarlet Monastery complex in northeastern Tirisfal Glades. Once serving as the burial grounds and crypts for Lordaeron's holy order, it has fallen into corruption and neglect, filled with tombs, mausoleums, and the unquiet dead.",al={"what is the graveyard","graveyard wing","scarlet graveyard"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened to the Scarlet Monastery Graveyard?",a="Originally a quiet resting place for honored priests and champions of Lordaeron, the grounds fell under the control of the Scarlet Crusade when the monastery was fortified against the Scourge. Rather than finding peaceful rest, the bodies buried here began to rise as undead, leaving the Crusade to wall off the blighted burial grounds.",al={"history of the graveyard","what happened here","graveyard origin"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who controls the Scarlet Monastery Graveyard?",a="While the Crusade claims the wider monastery complex, the Graveyard wing itself is largely abandoned to the restless undead. The fallen mage Thalnos, corrupted into a bloodthirsty, skeletal spellcaster, lords over the innermost tomb alongside scattered ghouls, ghosts, and wandering dead.",al={"who runs the graveyard","who is in charge here","graveyard leader"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Why is the Scarlet Monastery Graveyard abandoned and ruined?",a="The Crusade's fanatical holy power could not prevent the Scourge's plague from desecrating their dead. Unable to cleanse the rising corpses completely, the living crusaders withdrew to their fortified chapels and armories, leaving the burial grounds overgrown and overrun by reanimated corpses.",al={"why is the graveyard ruined","why is it abandoned","why neglected"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is the Scarlet Monastery Graveyard dangerous?",a="Yes. While less organized than the martial forces occupying the other monastery wings, the Graveyard is filled with aggressive undead, malicious spirits, and dark spellcasters like Bloodmage Thalnos who mercilessly assault any living intruders who trespass upon the tombs.",al={"is the graveyard dangerous","danger in the graveyard","how dangerous is the graveyard"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Scarlet Monastery Graveyard?",a="It serves as the dedicated burial grounds and cemetery of the Scarlet Monastery. It houses ancient crypts, mausoleums like Honor's Tomb, and the Forlorn Cloister where Lordaeron's holy defenders were traditionally laid to rest.",al={"why is it called the graveyard","graveyard name","why scarlet monastery graveyard"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="The damp, defiled soil of the Forlorn Cloister is one of the most reliable sources in northern Lordaeron for gathering Grave Moss.",["race:Undead"]="Forsaken spellcasters and apothecaries view the Graveyard as grim proof of the Crusade's hypocrisy: zealots who condemn the Forsaken while an undead bloodmage rots in their basement."},kw={"chamber of atonement","forlorn cloister","grave moss","graveyard","honor's tomb","scarlet monastery","thalnos"},rel={"zone:scarlet","subzone:grand-vestibule","npc:bloodmage-thalnos","subzone:forlorn-cloister","subzone:chamber-of-atonement","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge"},src={"Scarlet Monastery Graveyard"}}
E["subzone:scarlet-monastery-library"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarlet Monastery Library",z="scarlet",s="The Library is the eastern wing of the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades, once dedicated to holy scholarship and Lordaeron's priesthood. Now guarded by battle hounds and zealots, it houses ancient archives and rare tomes fiercely coveted by scholars and mages from both factions.",h="The Library is the eastern wing of the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades, once dedicated to holy...",sec={{t="Archives of Lordaeron",b="Before the Third War, the monastery served as a center for learning and enlightenment for Lordaeron's priesthood. The eastern cloisters housed vast archives of religious thought, historical records, and arcane treatises. When the Scarlet Crusade fortified the monastery against the Scourge, they retained these repositories, turning the quiet halls into an armed redoubt. Today, beastmasters run tracking hounds through the courtyards while battle-mages patrol the shelves, guarding historic volumes like the Compendium of the Fallen and ancient research on the Titans against outsiders.",sp=0},{t="Guardians of the Athenaeum",b="Breaching the Library requires navigating past Houndmaster Loksey in the Huntsman's Cloister, whose trained hounds sniff out infiltrators seeking passage into the inner chambers. Beyond the Gallery of Treasures lies the Athenaeum, overseen by Arcanist Doan. A formidable mage who wields devastating fire and protective sorcery, Doan studies in isolation, fiercely defending the Crusade's hoarded knowledge from any who venture into the heart of the complex.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Library within the Scarlet Monastery?",a="When entering the Grand Vestibule of the Scarlet Monastery complex in Tirisfal Glades, the Library wing is accessed through the right-most instance portal.",al={"library entrance","which door is library","how to find library wing"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are adventurers sent to the Library?",a="Scholars, priests, and mages from both the Alliance and Horde seek precious texts preserved within its walls. Important targets include the Compendium of the Fallen, Titan lore sought by Ironforge historians, and ancient magical manuals for rising arcanists.",al={"why go to library","library quests","what is in the library"},it="purpose"},{q="Who rules the Library wing?",a="The Library's inner sanctuary, the Athenaeum, is presided over by Arcanist Doan, a powerful scarlet spellcaster. The outer courtyard is secured by Houndmaster Loksey and his vicious tracking beasts.",al={"library boss","who is in charge of the library","who leads the library"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the Scarlet Key found here?",a="A lockbox in Arcanist Doan's Athenaeum holds the Scarlet Key, which is required to unlock the heavy iron doors granting entrance to the monastery's Armory and Cathedral wings.",al={"doan key","scarlet key drop","where is scarlet key"},it="item"},{q="What is the Scarlet Monastery Library?",a="The Library is the right-most wing of the sprawling Scarlet Monastery complex in Tirisfal Glades. Once a quiet center for study and clerical enlightenment in Lordaeron, it now houses the Scarlet Crusade's collected lore, military treasures, and hound kennels, divided into the Huntsman's Cloister, the Gallery of Treasures, and the Athenaeum.",al={"what is the library","scarlet library wing","monastery library overview"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened to the Scarlet Monastery Library?",a="The Library originally stood as part of a proud bastion of Lordaeron's priesthood, dedicated to learning, theological study, and enlightenment. When the undead Scourge tore through the kingdom in the Third War, surviving human zealots fortified the entire complex. They converted the peaceful repository of books and holy knowledge into an armed redoubt of the fanatical Scarlet Crusade.",al={"history of scarlet monastery library","library past","what happened here"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is the Scarlet Monastery Library dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The Library is garrisoned by zealous Scarlet soldiers, priests, and battle mages who view all outsiders as carriers of the Scourge plague to be eradicated on sight. Intruders must fight through trained attack hounds commanded by Houndmaster Loksey before facing the lethal sorcery of Arcanist Doan in the inner Athenaeum.",al={"is scarlet monastery library dangerous","library threats","how dangerous is the library"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The Athenaeum is an essential pilgrimage for ambitious mages seeking ancient rituals of power and to test their mettle against the destructive sorcery of Arcanist Doan.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Library holds sacred records of Lordaeron's fallen heroes and Titan histories that Ironforge's Hall of Explorers is desperate to recover from Crusader hands."},kw={"arcanist doan","athenaeum","compendium of the fallen","houndmaster loksey","library","scarlet key","scarlet monastery","tirisfal glades"},rel={"zone:scarlet","subzone:grand-vestibule","npc:arcanist-doan","npc:houndmaster-loksey","topic:scarlet-crusade","quest:1152","quest:1950"},src={"Scarlet Monastery Library"}}
E["subzone:terrace-of-repose"] = {t="subzone",n="Terrace of Repose",z="scarlet",s="The Terrace of Repose is a pristine courtyard garden located just outside the entrance to the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades. Maintained by the Scarlet Crusade, it stands as one of the few places in northern Lordaeron completely untouched by the Plague of Undeath, complete with green hedges and clean water.",h="The Terrace of Repose is a pristine courtyard garden located just outside the entrance to the Scarlet...",sec={{t="An Oasis in the Blight",b="Situated just north of the grand entrance into the Scarlet Monastery, the Terrace of Repose offers a surreal contrast to the rotting forests of Tirisfal Glades. While the rest of Lordaeron chokes under grey mist, corrupt soil, and stagnant bogs, this terrace boasts verdant, neatly pruned hedges and a functioning fountain fed by fresh, uncontaminated water. For the zealots of the Scarlet Crusade, the garden serves as physical proof of their divine righteousness and purity, a sacred bastion demonstrating that holy devotion can ward off the Scourge's corruption.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the grass and water clean here when Tirisfal is dead?",a="The Terrace of Repose has escaped the reach of the Plague of Undeath. Through constant vigilance and possibly their fierce devotion to the Holy Light, the Scarlet Crusade has preserved the soil, planted thriving hedges, and maintained a clear, fresh water supply entirely free of the surrounding rot.",al={"why is it green here","clean water scarlet monastery","terrace of repose uncorrupted"},it="place"},{q="Where exactly is the Terrace of Repose located?",a="It is situated immediately outside the entrance grounds of the Scarlet Monastery complex, in the northeastern hills of Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where is terrace of repose","terrace of repose location","monastery garden entrance"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What do the Crusaders use the terrace for?",a="Beyond serving as an approach to their fortified monastery, it provides a quiet sanctuary of uncorrupted earth where crusaders can rest, reflect, and behold an idealized glimpse of the kingdom of Lordaeron as it stood before the third war.",al={"scarlet crusade garden use","purpose of terrace of repose"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Terrace of Repose?",a="The Terrace of Repose is a serene courtyard situated just north of the Scarlet Monastery's main entrance. Kept under close guard by the Scarlet Crusade, it stands out as one of the few pristine spots left in northern Lordaeron, boasting manicured green hedges and fresh, flowing water untouched by the Scourge's rot.",al={"what is terrace of repose","terrace of repose scarlet monastery","about terrace of repose"},it="place",add=true},{q="Who controls the Terrace of Repose?",a="The Scarlet Crusade maintains and controls the terrace. Positioned right outside their sprawling monastery stronghold, the area serves as an outdoor retreat and defensible garden tended by Crusader sentries and clergy determined to preserve a corner of Lordaeron as it existed before the fall.",al={"who lives at terrace of repose","who controls terrace of repose","terrace of repose faction"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is the Terrace of Repose dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous to anyone outside the Scarlet Crusade. The terrace is heavily patrolled by zealous Crusaders who attack any intruders on sight, whether you are Forsaken, Horde, or unaligned travelers venturing too close to the monastery gates.",al={"is terrace of repose dangerous","terrace of repose threats","can i visit terrace of repose"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the pristine greenery of the terrace is a stark and bitter reminder of the living world that rejects them, maintained by mortal enemies who wish only to cleanse Lordaeron of their kind.",["class:Paladin"]="Seeing living flora and unpolluted water in Tirisfal is a powerful testament to the land's potential to heal, even if it is currently tended by unyielding fanatics."},kw={"fountain","hedges","plague of undeath","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","terrace of repose","tirisfal glades","uncorrupted"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:tirisfal","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Terrace of Repose"}}
E["subzone:whispering-gardens"] = {t="subzone",n="Whispering Gardens",z="scarlet",s="The Whispering Gardens occupy the terraced hillside just south of the Scarlet Monastery in northeastern Tirisfal Glades. Once a place of quiet contemplation, it became the site of a savage clash between early crusade defenders and a massive host of the Scourge. Today, crusaders patrol its overgrown pathways while the faint voices of the fallen linger in the air.",h="The Whispering Gardens occupy the terraced hillside just south of the Scarlet Monastery in northeastern...",sec={{t="A Battle Echoing in the Mist",b="Before the Scarlet Crusade fully retreated behind the fortress walls of the Monastery, a fierce battle erupted across these terraced slopes against an encroaching army of undead. The clash claimed countless lives on both sides. In the twilight, travelers through the gardens report hearing strange, soft murmurings on the wind—believed to be the restless echoes of the soldiers and priests who perished defending the holy grounds.",sp=0},{t="Crusader Outpost",b="Despite the haunting presence, the Scarlet Crusade maintains an active watch over the gardens. Scarlet scouts, magicians, and preservers guard the trails to intercept any intruders approaching from the lower glades. For the zealots within the nearby monastery, these overgrown steps serve as both a defensive bulwark and a solemn reminder of the ceaseless war against the undead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Whispering Gardens located?",a="The Whispering Gardens lie in northeastern Tirisfal Glades, blanketing the hillside immediately south of the entrance to the Scarlet Monastery.",al={"whispering gardens location","where is whispering gardens","how to get to whispering gardens"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are they called the Whispering Gardens?",a="The name comes from the faint, spectral murmurs heard in the twilight air, said to be the lingering spirits of the defenders and undead who fell in a bloody battle on these slopes.",al={"why is it called whispering gardens","what are the whispers","whispering gardens name"},it="name"},{q="What battle took place here?",a="A desperate battle was fought here between the early forces that became the Scarlet Crusade and an invading army of the Scourge. The combatants died in droves before the Scourge was halted outside the monastery.",al={"battle of whispering gardens","what happened at whispering gardens"},it="history"},{q="Who controls the gardens now?",a="The Scarlet Crusade controls the grounds. Scarlet scouts, preservers, and magicians patrol the terraces to secure the southern approach to their stronghold.",al={"who lives in whispering gardens","monsters in whispering gardens"},it="residents"},{q="What are the Whispering Gardens?",a="The Whispering Gardens are a somber hillside terrace situated in northeastern Tirisfal Glades, just south of the entrance to the Scarlet Monastery. Once peaceful grounds, the terrace now serves as an outer defensive post and staging ground for the zealous forces of the Scarlet Crusade overlooking the surrounding glades.",al={"what is whispering gardens","whispering gardens lore","what are whispering gardens"},it="place",add=true},{q="How dangerous are the Whispering Gardens?",a="They are extremely hazardous to any outsider. The Scarlet Crusade keeps an active guard throughout the terrace, stationing magicians, preservers, and scouts across the paths. Driven by fanatic paranoia, they execute anyone not sworn to their cause on sight, treating all outsiders as carriers of the undead taint.",al={"is whispering gardens dangerous","whispering gardens danger","threats in whispering gardens"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the gardens represent an active pocket of fanatical Scarlet resistance lingering right on the doorstep of Tirisfal, haunted by the very war that doomed Lordaeron.",["class:Priest"]="Priests walking the terraces can sense the lingering spiritual residue of holy defenders who met violent ends against the Scourge, their souls forever tied to the winds."},kw={"scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","scourge","tirisfal glades","whispering gardens","whispers"},rel={"zone:scarlet","zone:tirisfal","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:scourge","topic:light"},src={"Whispering Gardens"}}
E["zone:scarlet"] = {t="dungeon",n="Scarlet Monastery",z="scarlet",s="Perched in the northeastern hills of Tirisfal Glades, the Scarlet Monastery was once a peaceful sanctuary and center of learning for the Church of the Holy Light. Following the fall of Lordaeron, it was seized and heavily fortified by the Scarlet Crusade as their primary forward base in the west. Now, it stands as a sprawling stronghold divided into four wings, where fanatical zealots train, torture captives, and wage an uncompromising war against all outsiders.",h="Perched in the northeastern hills of Tirisfal Glades, the Scarlet Monastery was once a peaceful sanctuary and...",sec={{t="A Fallen Sanctuary",b="Before the Third War, the monastery served as a proud seat of Lordaeron's priesthood and a seminary for fledgling paladins of the Silver Hand, once cherished by Archbishop Alonsus Faol himself. Following the Scourge's devastation, surviving crusaders purged the halls of lingering undead and spiders, transforming the tranquil archives and courtyards into a fortified garrison. Driven by paranoia and grief, the Scarlet Crusade came to view all outsiders—living or undead, human or otherwise—as carriers of the plague who must be cleansed with fire.",sp=0},{t="The Four Wings",b="Past the monastery's Grand Vestibule lie four distinct quarters. The Graveyard is an unhallowed open-air terrace where fallen crusaders rise as undead abominations and torturers pry confessions from prisoners. The Library preserves precious theological texts and historical tomes, guarded by the renegade mage Arcanist Doan and his hounds. The Armory serves as a training ground where Scarlet weaponmasters like Herod drill fanatic recruits into ironclad warriors. Deepest within stands the Cathedral, the grand heart of the stronghold where the Crusade's leadership directs their crusade across the blighted north.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of the High Inquisitor",b="The inner sanctum of the Cathedral is commanded by Scarlet Commander Mograine and the monastery's true master, High Inquisitor Sally Whitemane. Defeating Whitemane strikes a critical blow to the Crusade's operational command in Tirisfal Glades. Her ability to channel blinding Holy Light and resurrect fallen champions made the garrison seem invincible to its devotees. Slaying her shatters the aura of divine mandate that fueled the monastery's zealotry, exposing the Crusade's leadership as mortal and severely weakening their campaign against the Forsaken and the neighboring lands.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is the Scarlet Crusade hostile to living Alliance adventurers?",a="The Crusade has succumbed to extreme madness and paranoia. In their eyes, anyone who does not wear their crimson tabard is a potential carrier of the Scourge plague. They no longer make distinctions between friend or foe, viewing all outsiders as tainted beings who must be purged before they can spread corruption.",al={"why do scarlets attack humans","scarlet crusade hostile alliance","why are they mad"},it="hostile"},{q="What happens when you defeat High Inquisitor Whitemane?",a="Defeating High Inquisitor Whitemane decapitates the Scarlet Crusade's western military leadership. As the spiritual leader of the monastery, her miraculous resurrection powers maintained troop morale and kept Commander Mograine fighting at her side. Her death removes the Crusade's most potent priestess in Tirisfal Glades, leaving the garrison disordered and severely diminishing their threat to the surrounding region.",al={"what does killing whitemane mean","whitemane defeated lore","cathedral ending"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is the Scarlet Key and where is it found?",a="The Scarlet Key is held deep within the Library wing of the monastery, kept inside Arcanist Doan's strongbox behind his personal study. Possessing this key is necessary to unlock the outer gates of both the Armory and the Cathedral wings.",al={"where is scarlet key","how to unlock armory and cathedral","monastery key"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why is Arcanist Doan in the Scarlet Monastery?",a="Arcanist Doan was a gifted human wizard from Dalaran who abandoned his fellow Kirin Tor magi to align with the Scarlet Crusade. Seeking seclusion to study rare manuscripts and master powerful fire and arcane magic, he took control of the monastery's extensive Library wing.",al={"who is arcanist doan","doan lore","mage in library"},it="identity"},{q="Who was Alexandros Mograine and how is he connected here?",a="Alexandros Mograine, the famed Ashbringer and former leader of the Silver Hand in Lordaeron, prayed and trained at the monastery during his youth. After the Third War, he made it a forward staging ground against the undead; his son Renault now commands the Cathedral alongside High Inquisitor Whitemane.",al={"mograine monastery history","ashbringer monastery","renault mograine father"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="What makes the Graveyard wing so different from the rest of the monastery?",a="While the rest of the monastery maintains an outward appearance of pristine devotion, the Graveyard is where the Crusade's fanaticism rots from within. It holds their brutal torture chambers run by Interrogator Vishas, while neglected crypts and restless dead are harvested or manipulated by fallen casters like Bloodmage Thalnos.",al={"why is graveyard undead","thalnos lore","interrogator vishas"},it="place"},{q="What is the Scarlet Monastery?",a="Perched in northeastern Tirisfal Glades, the Scarlet Monastery is a fortified sanctuary and the principal bastion of the Scarlet Crusade in the region. Once a peaceful cathedral complex devoted to the Holy Light and clerical learning, the stronghold has been converted into a heavily armed headquarters, training ground, and ideological redoubt for the Crusade's zealous campaign against undeath.",al={"what is scarlet monastery","scarlet monastery lore","about scarlet monastery"},it="place",add=true,nx={8}},{q="Was the Scarlet Monastery always theirs?",a="No. Before the fall of Lordaeron, it was known simply as the Old Monastery. Originally patronized by the noble House of Godwyn, it served as an archbishopric seat and seminary under Archbishop Alonsus Faol. Following the devastation of the Third War, surviving paladins reclaimed its halls from lingering Scourge infestations and renamed it the Scarlet Monastery.",al={"was scarlet monastery always crusade","history of scarlet monastery","who used to own scarlet monastery"},it="history",add=true,nx={9}},{q="Who built the Scarlet Monastery?",a="The Old Monastery was constructed as a sanctuary of the Church of the Holy Light under the sponsorship of the noble House of Godwyn. Its libraries and archives were curated for generations by archivists like Blake Godwyn, standing as a proud center of Lordaeron's priesthood and paladin training until the kingdom's collapse.",al={"who built the monastery","origins of the monastery"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Who are the Scarlet Crusade?",a="The Scarlet Crusade is a fanatical military order of human holy warriors and priests formed from remnants of the Knights of the Silver Hand. Consumed by grief and hatred following the Scourging of Lordaeron, they have committed themselves entirely to eradicating the undead, enforcing their mission with extreme ruthlessness and paranoia.",al={"who are scarlet crusade","what is the scarlet crusade","scarlet crusade lore"},it="threat",add=true,nx={11}},{q="Are the Scarlet Crusade human?",a="Yes, their ranks consist entirely of humans from the fallen realm of Lordaeron. They harbor fierce intolerance toward all non-human races, regardless of alliance or former ties, deeming outsiders unworthy or inherently tainted by the plague.",al={"are scarlet crusade only human","crusade race","is scarlet crusade human"},it="people",add=true},{q="Why am I attacking a church full of paladins?",a="Though they wear the trappings of holy orders and wield the Light, the Monastery's commanders have descended into violent extremism. Whether you answer the call of Raleigh the Devout to cleanse the order's corrupted leadership, or strike on behalf of Varimathras in the Undercity to neutralize an aggressive neighbor on his doorstep, you are there to break their military power.",al={"why attack scarlet monastery","why kill paladins here","reason to fight scarlet monastery"},it="purpose",add=true,nx={13,14}},{q="Are the Scarlet Crusade actually evil?",a="They began with a noble cause—purging Lordaeron of the undead Scourge. However, trauma and paranoia have warped their purpose entirely. They now torture innocent travelers, brand any outsider as plagued, and slaughter anyone not bearing their tabard, losing all moral sanity in the pursuit of purification.",al={"is scarlet crusade evil","are they bad guys","are crusaders evil"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Does the Alliance support the Scarlet Crusade?",a="Not officially. While some in Stormwind may harbor sympathy for Lordaeron's surviving holy warriors, the Crusade's indiscriminate hostility has severed formal ties. Adventurers and Alliance figures like Raleigh the Devout view their current commanders as mad zealots whose atrocities stain the honor of the Light.",al={"does alliance support crusade","is scarlet crusade alliance","alliance ties to scarlet crusade"},it="allies",add=true},{q="Who is in charge of the Scarlet Monastery?",a="The stronghold's military garrison answers to Scarlet Commander Renault Mograine, who commands a devoted force of warriors. However, the true spiritual and doctrinal master of the complex is High Inquisitor Sally Whitemane, a powerful priestess capable of reviving the fallen to fight in her name.",al={"who leads scarlet monastery","who runs the monastery","scarlet monastery leader"},it="in_charge",add=true,nx={16}},{q="Is the leader of the Monastery inside the Cathedral?",a="Yes. Both Scarlet Commander Mograine and High Inquisitor Whitemane reside within the Crusader's Chapel deep inside the Cathedral wing, guarded by an inner retinue of zealous defenders.",al={"where is whitemane","is whitemane in cathedral","cathedral boss location"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why does the Scarlet Crusade hate the Forsaken so much?",a="To the Crusade, all undead are abominations born of the plague that obliterated their families and homeland. They make no distinction between the mindless minions of the Scourge and the free-willed Forsaken occupying Capital City; both are seen as rotting usurpers that must be utterly cleansed in holy fire.",al={"crusade vs forsaken","why crusade hates undead","scarlet crusade forsaken feud"},it="history",add=true,nx={18}},{q="Were the Scarlet Crusaders and the Forsaken the same people once?",a="Yes. Most Crusaders and Forsaken were citizens, soldiers, or priests of the Kingdom of Lordaeron before the Third War. When the plague swept through, those who died and rose again became the undead, while the traumatized living fled or rallied together, turning former neighbors and kin into bitter, sworn enemies.",al={"did crusaders and forsaken know each other","were they both lordaeron citizens","lordaeron remnants"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Where did the Scarlet Crusade come from?",a="The Crusade arose from the surviving Knights of the Silver Hand and Lordaeron soldiers led by Highlord Alexandros Mograine and General Abbendis. Overwhelmed by the loss of their kingdom, the surviving leaders splintered: those advocating relentless, uncompromising zealotry formed the Scarlet Crusade, while moderates split away to found the Argent Dawn.",al={"origin of scarlet crusade","how was scarlet crusade founded","who started scarlet crusade"},it="history",add=true,nx={20}},{q="What was the Silver Hand?",a="The Knights of the Silver Hand were the legendary holy order of paladins founded during the Second War by Archbishop Alonsus Faol and Uther the Lightbringer. They served as the frontline champions of the Alliance and Lordaeron until Prince Arthas shattered their ranks during the Scourge's invasion.",al={"what were the silver hand","knights of the silver hand","silver hand paladins"},it="history",add=true},{q="Why do the Scarlet Crusade kill living humans too?",a="Deep paranoia has eroded the Crusade's grip on reality. They believe that any outsider could be a covert carrier of the undead plague. Anyone not wearing their uniform and submitting to their rigid authority is branded corrupted and sentenced to torture or death.",al={"why attack living humans","crusade kills humans","why do they kill their own kind"},it="threat",add=true},{q="Are the Scarlet Crusade a threat to Stormwind?",a="Not directly in terms of geographic conquest, as their efforts are anchored in the northern ruins of Lordaeron. However, their madness and willingness to murder any traveler makes them an active menace to Alliance citizens, ambassadors, and adventurers venturing anywhere near their territories.",al={"is scarlet crusade a threat to alliance","crusade vs stormwind","threat of scarlet crusade"},it="threat",add=true},{q="Why does everyone want me to go into the Scarlet Monastery?",a="Both factions have vital stakes in Tirisfal Glades. The Forsaken cannot tolerate a heavily armed zealot fortress right outside their capital, while Alliance figures seek to recover sacred texts, quell dangerous renegades, and bring justice to leadership gone mad.",al={"why am i sent to scarlet monastery","who wants the monastery dead","scarlet monastery quests reason"},it="why_me",add=true},{q="What is the Scarlet Monastery Library for?",a="The Library, which includes the Athenaeum and Gallery of Treasures, houses ancient Lordaeron scriptures, historical records, and arcane lore. It serves as both an intellectual archive and a secluded research sanctuary presided over by Arcanist Doan.",al={"library wing purpose","what are they doing in the library","scarlet monastery athenaeum"},it="place",add=true},{q="What are the Armory and Cathedral wings used for?",a="The Armory acts as the Crusade's martial heart, housing training grounds, barracks, and weapon caches overseen by Herod the Scarlet Champion. The Cathedral stands as the supreme spiritual sanctuary and command post, where Mograine drills elite troops and Whitemane delivers sermons and coordinates the Crusade's presence in Tirisfal.",al={"what are armory and cathedral for","purpose of armory sm","cathedral sm purpose"},it="place",add=true},{q="How did I end up in Scarlet Monastery?",a="You traveled to the far northeastern hills of Tirisfal Glades, pushing through the misty glades to the fortified seat of the Scarlet Crusade. Whether you crept up from the Undercity under orders from the Horde to dismantle a zealot threat on their doorstep, or marched north from Hillsbrad Foothills answering the call of disillusioned crusaders seeking to purge the Monastery's fanatical leadership, the path inevitably brought you before this heavily guarded complex.",al={"how did i get here","how did i get to scarlet monastery","why did i come here"},it="arrival",add=true},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Scarlet Monastery?",a="You are here to breach the Crusade's four wings and break their hold over the region. Depending on who sent you, you may be hunting down fallen leadership like Scarlet Commander Mograine and High Inquisitor Whitemane, uncovering lost tomes and lore within the library, gathering hearts of zeal for the Royal Apothecary Society, or recovering holy artifacts and slaying corrupted leaders who brand anyone outside their ranks as plagued undead.",al={"what am i doing here","why am i here","what is my mission here"},it="purpose",add=true}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The monastery once served as a sacred seminary where the first paladins of the Silver Hand trained and prayed, making its descent into crimson zealotry a tragic reminder of how devotion can curdle into madness.",["class:Priest"]="Originally dedicated to Archbishop Alonsus Faol and the Church of the Holy Light, its grand chapels demonstrate how holy power can still be wielded by mortals twisted by hatred and vengeance.",["race:Undead"]="Perched on the border of Tirisfal Glades, the Scarlet Monastery represents an existential threat to the Forsaken, staging spies into Deathknell and torturing captured undead within its dungeons.",["class:Mage"]="The Library wing houses rare historical and theological tomes guarded by Arcanist Doan, a former Dalaran scholar who defected to the Crusade's cause."},kw={"armory","cathedral","doan","graveyard","herod","library","mograine","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","tirisfal glades","whitemane"},rel={"subzone:scarlet-monastery-cathedral","subzone:scarlet-monastery-armory","subzone:scarlet-monastery-library","subzone:scarlet-monastery-graveyard","npc:sally-whitemane","npc:scarlet-commander-mograine","npc:arcanist-doan","topic:scarlet-crusade"},m={levels="26-45"},src={"Scarlet Monastery","Scarlet Monastery"}}
